hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4801","Ubayd ibn Kathir at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Salih ibn Hayy narrated to us, from his uncle al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except his nephew; Muhammad ibn al-Junayd is alone in it."
"4802","Ubayd ibn Kathir at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ziyad al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Shaddad, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reviles Ammar, Allah reviles him; and whoever hates Ammar, Allah hates him. Al-Abbas ibn al-Hasan did not narrate any hadith with a chain except this one; al-Walid ibn Hammad is alone in it."
"4803","Ubayd ibn Kathir at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: My brother Ziyad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any slave who marries without the permission of his masters is a fornicator. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Ayyub except Ziyad ibn al-Hasan; Yahya ibn al-Hasan is alone in it."
"4804","Ubayd ibn Kathir at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Atiyya al-Awfi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Khosrow perishes there will be no Khosrow after him, and when Caesar perishes there will be no Caesar after him; and by Him in whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the path of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Aban ibn Taghlib except Ibn al-Ajlah; Minjab is alone in it."
"4805","Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Subayh az-Zayyat al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur as-Saluli narrated to us, from Huraym ibn Sufyan al-Bajali, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of youths, upon you is marriage; whoever cannot, upon him is fasting, for it is a restraint for him. No one narrated this hadith from Huraym ibn Sufyan except Ishaq ibn Mansur."
"4806","Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Subayh az-Zayyat narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yunus al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from Qutba ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: and the palm trees, towering, with the letter sad. No one said in this hadith with the letter sad except Hisham ibn Yunus."
"4807","Ubayd ibn Khalaf al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Isa al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his brother whose belly had swollen with dropsy, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother's belly has swollen; I took him to the doctors and they ordered cauterization, shall I cauterize him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not cauterize him, and return him to his family. A camel passed by him and struck his belly, so it shrank; he brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Know that if you had taken him to the doctors you would have said: fire healed him. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Abdullah ibn Isa."
"4808","Ubayd ibn Khalaf al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad an-Naqid narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed the last of what was preserved of the speech of Prophethood is: if you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil except Layth; Mu'tamir is alone in it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Mas'ud except with this chain."
"4809","Ubayd ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: al-Mughira ibn Isma'il ibn Ayyub ibn Salama narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd ar-Rahman az-Zuhri, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who pursues a woman unlawfully, may he marry her mother? Or pursues the mother unlawfully, may he marry her daughter? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The unlawful does not forbid the lawful; only what is through a lawful marriage forbids. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except al-Mughira ibn Isma'il; Abdullah ibn Nafi' is alone in it."
"4810","Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Kishwari as-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muhammad ibn Thawr; his son is alone in it."
"4811","Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Kishwari as-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Ghassan as-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Sufyan ath-Thawri, from Ma'mar, from az-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go around his wives with one bath. No one narrated this hadith from ath-Thawri, from Ma'mar, from az-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, except Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam; and Abu Nu'aym and others narrated it from Sufyan ath-Thawri, from Ma'mar, from Qatada."
"4812","Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Kishwari narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah ibn Hamza as-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd and Abdur-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things do not break the fast of one fasting: vomiting, cupping, and a wet dream. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Sa'd except Yahya ibn Thabit al-Jazari; Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah is alone in it."
"4813","Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Kishwari narrated to us, he said: Abd as-Salam ibn Ilyas as-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn ash-Sharud narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas, Abdullah ibn Umar, and Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every intoxicant is wine, and whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Malik and Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Bakr ibn ash-Sharud."
"4814","Ubayd ibn Abdillah ibn Jahsh al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Junada ibn Marwan al-Azdi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn an-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to swear I would fulfill it; indeed the most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah are the herders of the sun and the moon, meaning the mu'adhdhins; and they will be known on the Day of Resurrection by the length of their necks."
"4815","Ubayd ibn Abdillah ibn Jahsh narrated to us, he said: Junada ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn an-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day holding Abu Dharr's hand, and said: O Abu Dharr, do you know that before us is a steep pass which none ascends except the light-burdened? A man said: O Messenger of Allah, am I of the light-burdened or of the heavy-burdened? He said: Do you have food for a day? He said: Yes. And food for tomorrow? He said: Yes. And food for the day after tomorrow? He said: No. He said: If you had food for three days you would be of the heavy-burdened."
"4816","Ubayd ibn Abdillah ibn Jahsh narrated to us, he said: Junada ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn an-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: One who persists in usury is like a worshipper of an idol, and one who persists in wine is like a worshipper of an idol."
"4817","Ubayd ibn Abdillah ibn Jahsh narrated to us, he said: Junada ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn an-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to keep the night alive with eight rak'as, their bowing like their recitation and their prostration like their recitation, and he would give salam between every two rak'as."
"4818","Ubayd ibn Abdillah ibn Jahsh narrated to us, he said: Junada ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn an-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not honor our elder, have mercy on our young, befriend for our sake, and visit."
"4819","Ubayd ibn Abdillah ibn Jahsh narrated to us, he said: Junada ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn an-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the rich from the poor on the Day of Resurrection; they will say: Our Lord, they wronged us of our rights which You obligated for us upon them. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: By My might and majesty, I will surely bring you near and distance them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And those in whose wealth is a known right, for the asker and the deprived. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except al-Harith ibn an-Nu'man."
"4820","Abd as-Samad ibn Muhammad al-Aynuni al-Maqdisi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hubayra Muhammad ibn al-Walid ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Salama ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn as-Simt narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gesture in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Yazid ibn as-Simt; Salama ibn Bishr is alone in it."
"4821","Abd as-Samad ibn Muhammad al-Aynuni narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Adam ibn Abi Iyas al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from ash-Sha'bi, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever conceals beneficial knowledge will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire. None put ash-Sha'bi between Jabir and Ata in this hadith except Shayban; Adam is alone in it."
"4822","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr al-Makhzumi al-Misri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Mufaddal ibn Faddala narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsa, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Friday is obligatory upon every one who has reached puberty, and bathing is upon whoever goes to Friday prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Hafsa, except Bukayr ibn Abdillah, nor from Bukayr except Ayyash ibn Abbas; Mufaddal ibn Faddala is alone in it."
"4823","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Mufaddal ibn Faddala narrated to us, from Abu Urwa, from Abu Ammar, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah will not leave any Muslim on Friday except that He forgives him. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Yahya ibn Bukayr is alone in it. In my view Abu Urwa is Ma'mar ibn Rashid, and Abu Ammar is Ziyad an-Numayri."
"4824","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn an-Nayl al-Fihri narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while people were praying after dawn had risen, and said: There is no prayer after dawn has risen except two rak'as. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn an-Nayl except al-Layth ibn Sa'd."
"4825","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ya'qub ibn Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from al-Muttalib, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, upon him be peace, kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir. This hadith is not narrated from Zayd ibn Thabit except with this chain; Ya'qub ibn Abd ar-Rahman is alone in it."
"4826","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj narrated to me, from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf, that Zaynab bint Abi Salama informed him, from her mother Umm Salama, that a woman from Aslam called Subay'a was under a husband of hers, and he died leaving her pregnant; Abu as-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak proposed to her and she refused to marry him, so he said: It is not right for you to marry until you complete the longer of the two terms. She remained about twenty nights, then gave birth, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, and he said to her: Marry. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'raj except Ibn Lahi'a."
"4827","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Guarding a day in the path of Allah is better than fasting a day and standing it in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Habib except Ibn Lahi'a."
"4828","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Umm Salama, that Zaynab bint Rasulillah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out emigrating, asked permission of Abu al-As ibn Rabi', her husband, to go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he permitted her, so she came to him. Then Abu al-As caught up at Madina and sent to her: take for me protection from your father. She went out and showed her head from the door of her chamber while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the dawn prayer leading the people, and said: O people, I am Zaynab bint Rasulillah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I have granted protection to Abu al-As. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer he said: O people, I did not know of this until you heard it; know that the lowest of the Muslims grants protection on their behalf. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salama except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'a is alone in it."
"4829","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sawada narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ma'afiri, from Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab gave Abdullah ibn as-Sa'di a thousand dinars, but he refused to accept it. Umar said to him: I will say to you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me; he said: When Allah drives provision to you without asking and without the soul aspiring to it, take it, for Allah has given it to you. No one narrated this hadith from Qabisa ibn Dhu'ayb except Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ma'afiri, nor from Abdullah ibn Yazid except Bakr ibn Sawada; Ibn Lahi'a is alone in it."
"4830","Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salama, from an-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade renting out land. No one narrated this hadith from an-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash except Abdullah ibn Abi Salama, nor from Abdullah ibn Abi Salama except Bukayr ibn Abdillah; Ibn Lahi'a is alone in it."
"4831","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Adi Abu Nu'aym al-Jurjani, in the year 288, narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Raja al-Jurjani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Tayba narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever guards a day in the path of Allah, Allah will place between him and the Fire seven trenches, each trench like seven heavens and seven earths."
"4832","And from Jabir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will place between him and the Fire a trench like what is between the heaven and the earth."
"4833","And from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Umm Hani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed my umma will not be disgraced as long as they uphold the fasting of Ramadan. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their disgrace in neglecting the month of Ramadan? He said: Violating the sacred things in it; whoever does adultery in it or drinks wine, Allah curses him and those in the heavens until the like of it of the year. If he dies before reaching the month of Ramadan, he has no good deed with Allah by which to shield himself from the Fire. So fear the month of Ramadan, for good deeds are multiplied in it as they are not multiplied in other than it, and likewise evil deeds. No one narrated these hadiths from al-A'mash except Abu Tayba; his son is alone in them."
"4834","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Jurjani Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Tayba narrated to us, he said: Anbasa ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Ali: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the last ten entered, would exert himself and his family would exert themselves. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, except Anbasa; Ahmad ibn Abi Tayba is alone in it."
"4835","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Sayyar al-Bahili al-Jurjani narrated to us, from Khalaf ibn Khalifa, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my umma in its early morning, and make it Thursday. No one narrated this hadith from Muharib except Khalaf ibn Khalifa; Affan ibn Sayyar is alone in it."
"4836","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad Abu Nu'aym al-Jurjani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Jurjani narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Sa'id al-Jurjani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ath-Thawri narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr, and Maghrib and Isha, without fear or rain. It was said: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended not to burden his umma."
"4837","And from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr at every part of the night, its beginning, middle, and end; then his witr ended at dawn."
"4838","And from Sufyan, from Asim, from ash-Sha'bi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried al-Hasan and al-Husayn and Abdullah ibn Ja'far on a mount. No one narrated these hadiths from Sufyan except Sa'd ibn Sa'id; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim is alone in them."
"4839","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Jurjani Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Tayba narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Talha ibn Amr, from Ata, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you turn away the beggar three times, there is no blame on you if you add to it."
"4840","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Tayba narrated to us, he said: ar-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people gather then disperse without the remembrance of Allah except that they disperse from what is fouler than a carcass."
"4841","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad Abu Nu'aym al-Jurjani narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Raja al-Jurjani narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim and al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfa, who said: Umar said: Which of you remembers what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about tribulation? Hudhayfa said: I do: a man's tribulation in his family and wealth is expiated by prayer, charity, enjoining good and forbidding evil. He said: I did not ask you about this; I asked you about the tribulation that surges like the waves of the sea. He said: Between you and it is a closed door. He said: Will that door be opened or broken? He said: Rather it will be broken. He said: Then it will never be closed."
"4842","Abd as-Salam ibn Sahl as-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other than it, except the Sacred Mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, nor did anyone narrate it from Sa'id except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata."
"4843","Abd as-Salam ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumayla narrated to us, from Abu Tayba, he said: Abu Mijlaz narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk and drinks from silver is not of us; and whoever alienates a woman against her husband, or a slave against his masters, is not of us. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Abu Tumayla is alone in it."
"4844","Abd as-Salam ibn Sahl as-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr Abu Umar narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that a man prayed behind the rows alone, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to repeat the prayer. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Abu Yahya al-Himmani is alone in it."
"4845","Abd as-Salam ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim at-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayya, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Duba'a while she was ill, and said: Perform Hajj and stipulate, saying: O Allah, my place of release is where You detain me. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Umayya except Muhammad ibn Muslim; Imran ibn Aban is alone in it."
"4846","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abi Amir as-Sihlini al-Khath'ami narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated to us, he said: Ikrima ibn Ammar al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Abu Zumayl Simak al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Marthad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In your enjoining good and forbidding evil there is charity for you; your removing harm from the road is charity for you; your pouring from your bucket into your brother's bucket is charity for you; and your smiling. None raised this hadith from Ikrima ibn Ammar except an-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi, Abu Hudhayfa, and Abdullah ibn Raja al-Ghudani."
"4847","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abi Amir as-Sihlini al-Khath'ami narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated to us, he said: Ikrima ibn Ammar al-Ijli narrated to us, from Ata, freedman of as-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, who said: I saw my master as-Sa'ib, his beard white and his head black. I said: O my master, why does your head not turn white? He said: My head will never turn white. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed while I was a boy playing with the boys; he greeted the boys and I was among them, so I returned the greeting among the boys. He called me and said: What is your name? I said: as-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, nephew of Namir. He placed his hand on my head and said: May Allah bless you. So the place of the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will never turn white. No one narrated this hadith from Ata, freedman of as-Sa'ib, except Ikrima ibn Ammar; an-Nadr ibn Muhammad is alone in it, and it is not narrated from as-Sa'ib except with this chain."
"4848","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha ar-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Atiyya narrated to us, he said: Sa''ad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ata, from Abdullah ibn Burayda, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali ibn Abi Talib and Khalid ibn al-Walid, each of them alone, and joined them, saying: When you meet, Ali is in charge over you. He said: They took right and left; Ali entered and went far, took captives, and took a slave girl from the captives. Burayda said: I was of the severest of people in hatred of Ali. A man came to Khalid ibn al-Walid and mentioned that he had taken a slave girl from the fifth; he said: What is this? Then another came, then another, then reports followed upon that. Khalid called me and said: O Burayda, you know what was done; go with this letter of mine to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He wrote to him, so I went with his letter until I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he took the letter in his left hand, and he was as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: he neither reads nor writes. He said: When I spoke I would lower my head until I finished my need, so I lowered my head and spoke, and I fell upon Ali until I finished. Then I raised my head and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angry with an anger the like of which I had not seen him angry except on the day of Qurayza and an-Nadir. He looked at me and said: O Burayda, love Ali, for he only does what he is commanded. He said: I stood, and there was no one among people more beloved to me than him. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Ata except Sa''ad ibn Sulayman, nor did anyone narrate it from Sa''ad except Hasan ibn Atiyya; Abu Kurayb is alone in it."
"4849","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha ar-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, from his father, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, who said: Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, purify me. He said: Woe to you, return and ask Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. He said: He returned a short distance, then came and said: O Messenger of Allah, purify me. He said the like of that to him until when it was the fourth time, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: From what shall I purify you? He said: From adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is he mad? He was informed that he was not mad. He said: Smell him. A man stood and smelled him and found no smell of wine from him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you commit adultery? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding him and he was stoned. People were two parties about him: one saying: He has perished upon the worst of deeds, his sin has encompassed him; and one saying: There is no repentance better than the repentance of one who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed his hand in his hand, then said: Kill me with stones. They remained upon that for two or three days. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while they were sitting; he greeted, then sat and said: Ask forgiveness for Ma'iz ibn Malik. They said: May Allah forgive Ma'iz. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has repented a repentance which, if divided among an umma, would encompass them. Then a woman from Ghamid of al-Azd came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, purify me. He said: Return, ask Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. She said: I see you want to turn me back as you turned back Ma'iz ibn Malik? He said: From what shall I purify you? She said: She is pregnant from adultery. He said: Did you commit adultery? She said: Yes. He said: Then I will not stone you until you deliver what is in your belly. A man of the Ansar took charge of her until she delivered; he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The Ghamidi woman has delivered. He said: Then I will not stone her and leave her child small with none to suckle him. A man of the Ansar stood and said: Its suckling is upon me, O Messenger of Allah. So he stoned her. No one narrated this hadith from Ghaylan ibn Jami' except Ya'la ibn al-Harith; his son Yahya is alone in it."
"4850","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Mukhtar ibn Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Muslim Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la ibn Amir, who said: Abu Abd ar-Rahman as-Sulami said: I entered the mosque while the Commander of the Believers, Ali, was on the pulpit saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah revealed to a prophet of the prophets of the Children of Isra'il: say to the obedient of your umma: let them not rely upon their deeds, for I do not settle the account with a servant on the Day of Resurrection then wish to punish him except that I punish him; and say to the sinful of your umma: let them not despair, for I forgive great sins and do not care. There is no people of a village, nor of a city, nor of a land, nor a man in particular, nor a woman, who is toward Me upon what I love except that I am toward him upon what he loves. And there is no city, nor people of a land, nor a man in particular, nor a woman, who is toward Me upon what I love, then turns from what I love to what I hate, except that I turn for him from what he loves to what he hates. And there is no people of a village, nor of a city, nor of a land, nor a man in particular, nor a woman, who is toward Me upon what I hate then turns toward Me from what I hate to what I love, except that I turn for him from what he hates to what he loves. None of me is one who takes omens or has omens taken for him, or soothsayes or has soothsaying done for him, or does magic or has magic done for him; I am only I and My creation, and all My creation is Mine. None narrates this hadith from Abu Abd ar-Rahman as-Sulami except Abd al-A'la; Isa ibn Muslim is alone in it, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"4851","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Bishr al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn al-Alawi narrated to us, from his father, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril said to me: O Muhammad, love whom you wish, for you will part from him; do what you wish, for you will meet it; live as you wish, for you will die. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril made the sermon concise for me."
"4852","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, nothing joined to anything is better than forbearance joined to knowledge."
"4853","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of intellect after faith is endearing oneself to people."
"4854","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, whoever does not have them is not of me nor of Allah. It was said: What are they? He said: Forbearance repelling the ignorance of the ignorant, or good character by which he lives among people, or piety restraining him from Allah's disobedience."
"4855","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Rawaha narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Jasr ibn Farqad, from al-Hasan, who said: I asked Imran ibn Husayn and Abu Hurayra about a verse of Allah's Book, about His saying: and pleasant dwellings in Gardens of Eden? They said: You have fallen upon the expert; we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: A palace in Paradise of pearl, in it seventy houses of red ruby, in each house seventy rooms of green emerald, in each room seventy beds. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Jasr ibn Farqad."
"4856","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubayda al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jami' al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abu Na'ama narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Umayr, from Utba ibn Ghazwan as-Sulami, who said: We used to witness fighting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when the sun declined he would say to us: Charge, so we charged. This hadith is not narrated from Utba ibn Ghazwan except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Jami' is alone in it."
"4857","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jami' al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not settle in kufur, for they are like graves, meaning villages."
"4858","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jami' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not stretch tent ropes for the desert, for in the desert is harshness; and Allah's Hand is over the community, and Allah does not care for the straying of whoever strays. Let not two ride a mount more than two, and do not strike the faces of beasts, for everything glorifies with His praise. And do not name your sons and brothers al-Hakam, nor Abu al-Hakam, for Allah is al-Hakam. These two hadiths are not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Jami' is alone in them."
"4859","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubayd al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Hawthara ibn Ashras al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Marthad al-Adawi narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd al-Adawi, from Mu'adha al-Adawiyya, that A'isha said: O company of women, order your husbands to wash from themselves the trace of urine and stool, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash from himself the trace of urine and stool, and I am shy to say it to them. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Suwayd except Ibrahim ibn Marthad al-Adawi; Hawthara ibn Ashras is alone in it."
"4860","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubayda al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: Habib ibn al-Harith came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who commits sins repeatedly. He said: Repent to Allah, O Habib. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I repent then return. He said: Every time you sin, repent. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then my sins will be many. He said: Allah's pardon is greater than your sins, O Habib ibn al-Harith. This hadith is not narrated from Hisham ibn Urwa except with this chain; Isa ibn Ibrahim is alone in it."
"4861","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubayda narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabala narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A people ruled by a woman will never prosper. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Samura except with this chain; Abdur-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Jabala is alone in it."
"4862","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim Abu Ubayda narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar ar-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd ar-Rahman at-Tara'ifi al-Harrani narrated to us, from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi' al-Uqayli, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I entered with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) into a garden of some Ansar; I handed him a green unripe date and he ate it, then said: O Ibn Umar, this is the first food I have eaten in three days. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except al-Wazi' ibn Nafi'."
"4863","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu ar-Rabi' az-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd ar-Rahman ad-Dalani, from Firas, from ash-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abdullah, regarding a man who married a woman, died leaving her without consummating with her and without fixing a dower for her, he said: She has the full dower, upon her is the waiting period, and for her is inheritance. Ma'qil ibn Sinan said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judge so regarding Barwa' bint Washiq. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid ad-Dalani except al-Muharibi."
"4864","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Abu ar-Rabi' as-Samman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cleanse with cold water, for it is a cure for piles. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwa except Abu ar-Rabi' as-Samman; Ammar is alone in it."
"4865","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Miskin al-Uswari narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Amir ash-Sha'bi, from Fatima bint Qays, who said: I heard the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) call: The prayer is gathering. I went out among women of the Ansar until we came to the mosque; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Zuhr prayer, then ascended the pulpit, faced us smiling, then said: By Allah, I did not gather you for a desired talk nor a feared one, except for a talk Tamim ad-Dari told me. He came to me, accepted Islam and pledged; he informed me that he sailed with thirty men of Lakhm and Judham, two tribes of the Arabs of Yemen, and they met the sea when it was agitated; the waves played with them a month, then cast them near sunset upon an island of the islands of the sea. He said: There we were met by a hairy beast; we could not tell its front from its back. We said: Who are you, O beast? Allah permitted, and it spoke to us with an eloquent fluent tongue, saying: I am al-Jassasa. We said: What is al-Jassasa? It said: Away from me; upon you is that monastery at the far end of the island, for in it is a man most eager for your news. We came to the monastery, and there we were met by a man, the greatest man I ever saw in creation, the stoutest in body; his right eye was wiped as if his eye were phlegm on a plastered wall; his hands were chained to his neck; his legs were bound with fetters from his knees to his feet. We said to him: Who are you, O man? He said: As for my news, you have come to know of it; inform me of your news. What cast you upon this island? No human has reached this island since I came to be in it. He said to us: Inform me of the Lake of Tiberias, what has become of it? We said to him: About which of its matters do you ask? He said: Has its water dried? Have its wonders appeared? We said: No, by Allah. He said: It will be. Then he was silent a while, then said: Inform me of the spring of Zughar, what has become of it? We said: About which of its matters do you ask? He said: Do its people plough upon it? We said to him: Yes. He said: Its water will soon sink, so its people will not plough upon it. Then he was silent a while, then said: Inform me of the palms of Baysan, what has become of them? We said: About which of their matters do you ask? He said: Do they bear fruit? We said: Yes. He said: They will soon not bear fruit. Then he was silent a while, then said: Inform me of the unlettered Prophet, what has become of him? We said: About which of his matters do you ask? He said: Has he appeared? We said: Yes. He said: What did the Arabs do with him? We said: Of them are those who fought him, and of them are those who believed him. He said: Whoever believed him, it is better for him, three times. We said: Inform us of your news, O man? He said: Do you not know me? We said: Had we known you we would not have asked you. He said: I am the Dajjal; soon I will be permitted to come out. When I come out I will tread all the land of the Arabs except Makka and Tayba; whenever I intend them an angel meets me with a drawn sword in his hand and turns me back from them. Abu al-Ashhab said: Amir said: Fatima said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, then he said: Shall I not inform you, this is Tayba, three times. Then he said: Shall I not inform you that he is in the sea of Sham? Then he swooned a while, then it left him, then he said: Rather he is in the sea of Yemen. Then he swooned a while, then it left him, and said: He is in the sea of Iraq, three times. He will come out when he comes out from a town called Asbahan, from a village of its villages called Rustuqbadh; he will come out with seventy thousand at his front, upon them sijan; with him are two rivers: a river of water and a river of fire. Whoever of you reaches that, if he is told: enter the water, let him not enter it, for it is fire; and when he is told: enter the fire, let him enter it, for it is water. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ashhab except Sayf ibn Miskin; Abu Ubayda is alone in it."
"4866","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from al-Muntasir ibn Umara, from his father, from his grandfather, and his grandfather was Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the time draws near, wearing tayalisas will be many, trade will be many, wealth will be many, the owner of wealth will be honored for his wealth, indecency will be many, rule of children will be, corruption will be many, the ruler will be unjust, cheating in measure and weight, a man raising a puppy will be better for him than raising a child, the elder will not be honored nor the young shown mercy, children of adultery will be many, until a man will approach a woman on the roadside; the best of them in that time will say: If only you withdrew from the road. They wear sheep skins over wolf hearts; the best of them in that time is the flatterer."
"4867","Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sayf ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Utayy as-Sa'di; Utayy said: I went out seeking knowledge until I came to Kufa; there I found Abdullah ibn Mas'ud among the people of Kufa. I asked about him and was guided to him; he was in its great mosque. I came to him and said: O Abu Abd ar-Rahman, I have come traveling to you seeking knowledge from you; perhaps Allah will benefit us by it after you. He said to me: From where is the man? I said: A man of Basra. He said: From whom? I said: From this tribe of Banu Sa'd. He said to me: O Sa'di, I will narrate among you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not guide you to a people: much wealth, much might, you will take from them much wealth readily, or he said: much? He said: Who are they? He said: This tribe of Banu Sa'd, of the people of the sands. The Messenger of Allah said: Hush, for Banu Sa'd have a great share with Allah. Ask, O Sa'di. I said: O Abu Abd ar-Rahman, is there a knowledge of the Hour by which the Hour is known? He was reclining, then sat up and said: O Sa'di, you asked me what I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there a knowledge of the Hour by which the Hour is known? He said: Yes, O Ibn Mas'ud, indeed the Hour has signs, and indeed the Hour has portents. Know that of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that the child will be anger, and rain will be scorching heat, and nobles will overflow in abundance. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that the traitor will be trusted and the trustworthy betrayed. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that dishes will be joined and kinship cut. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that every tribe will be led by its hypocrites, and every market by its wicked. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that prayer niches will be distorted and hearts ruined. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that the believer in the tribe will be more lowly than small change. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that men will suffice with men and women with women. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is the rule of children and consultation of women. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that mosques will be many and pulpits high. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that the ruin of the world will be built and its building ruined. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that instruments and pride and drinking wine will appear. O Ibn Mas'ud, of the signs of the Hour and its portents is that children of adultery will be many. I said: O Abu Abd ar-Rahman, while they are Muslims? He said: Yes. I said: O Abu Abd ar-Rahman, while the Qur'an is among them? He said: Yes. I said: O Abu Abd ar-Rahman, how is that? He said: A time will come upon people when a man divorces a woman, then denies her divorce, and remains upon her; they are two adulterers as long as they remain. None narrated these two hadiths from Mubarak ibn Fadala except Sayf ibn Miskin."
"4868","Abd al-Kabir ibn Umar al-Khattabi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Mudrik ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: Shihab ibn Ma'mar al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Hayyan ibn Ubaydillah al-Adawi narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from A'isha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Hayyan ibn Ubaydillah; Shihab ibn Ma'mar is alone in it."
"4869","Abd al-Kabir ibn Umar al-Khattabi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abbad al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far ar-Razi narrated to us, from ar-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and saw in the mosque a man not completing his bowing nor his prostration, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of a man who does not complete bowing and prostration is not accepted. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ja'far ar-Razi except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr; Ibrahim ibn Abbad is alone in it."
"4870","Abd al-Kabir ibn Umar al-Khattabi narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: as-Sakan ibn Abi as-Sakan Abu Amr al-Burjumi narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Humayd at-Tawil, he said: I think I heard it from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being led between two men, and said: What is this? They said: He vowed to perform Hajj walking. He said: Allah has no need of this one killing himself; order him to ride. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except as-Sakan al-Burjumi; Azhar ibn Jamil is alone in it."
"4871","Abd al-Kabir ibn Muhammad al-Ansari Abu Umayr, of the offspring of Anas ibn Malik, narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud ash-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever raises a child until he says: there is no god but Allah, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not call him to account. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwa except Isa ibn Yunus; Sulayman ibn Dawud is alone in it."
"4872","Abd al-Aziz ibn Ya'qub Abu al-Asbagh al-Qaysarani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise eat and drink, and do not spit, nor blow their noses, nor defecate, nor urinate; their food is belching, and sweat like the sweat of musk. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except al-Firyabi and Abu Bakr al-Hanafi."
"4873","Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn ibn Bakr ibn ash-Sharud narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Ja'far ibn Sulayman, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked: Is slaughtering only in the throat and the chest? He said: Had you stabbed her in her thigh it would have sufficed you. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far ibn Sulayman except Bakr ibn ash-Sharud, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"4874","Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Hilal as-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Bakkar ibn Yahya, nephew of Hammam, narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatada say: I asked Anas ibn Malik: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited he would prolong his voice with prolongation. No one narrated this hadith from Harb ibn Shaddad except Bakkar ibn Yahya; Bishr ibn Hilal is alone in it."
"4875","Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man fasts for Allah voluntarily, then is given the earth full of gold, he will not receive his reward in full before the Day of Reckoning."
"4876","Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is Mine, and I reward for it; and the breath of the fasting one's mouth is sweeter with Allah than the scent of musk. None narrated these two hadiths from Layth except Abd al-Warith; Bishr ibn Hilal is alone in them."
"4877","Abd al-Aziz ibn Sulayman al-Harmali al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ka'b al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Imran ibn Sulayman, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined me with three: the Duha prayer, not to sleep except upon witr, and to fast three days of every month. No one narrated this hadith from Imran ibn Sulayman, who is al-Qabbi, except Isa ibn Yunus."
"4878","Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub as-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Hujr al-Madari, from Zayd ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Umra is for the heir. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Uthman ibn Abd ar-Rahman; Abu Kamil is alone in it."
"4879","Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Abd as-Salam ibn Umar al-Jinni narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Mutarrif ibn Abdillah ibn ash-Shikhkhir, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, that a man fought a man, and one of them bit the other's hand; the man pulled his hand away and the biter's front tooth fell out. They were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Does one of you bite his brother as the stallion bites? No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Maymuna except his son Rawh; Abd as-Salam ibn Umar is alone in it."
"4880","Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Harbi narrated to us, he said: Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Uqayl and Qurra, from az-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you goes to relieve himself, let him not face the qibla nor turn his back to it; face east and west. No one narrated this hadith from Qurra ibn Abd ar-Rahman except Rushdin ibn Sa'd."
"4881","Abdus ibn Dizawayh ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiya ibn Hafs narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Hisham, from Qatada, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting Arafa expiates two years: a past year and a coming year; and the day of Ashura expiates a year. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except al-Hakam ibn Hisham, nor from al-Hakam except Mu'awiya ibn Hafs; Muhammad ibn Musaffa is alone in it."
"4882","Abdus ibn Dizawayh ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir ibn Mismar narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from the freedman of al-Huraqa, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah recited Ta-Ha and Ya-Sin a thousand years before creating Adam; when the angels heard the Qur'an they said: Blessed is an umma upon which this descends, blessed are bellies carrying this, and blessed are tongues speaking with this. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"4883","Abdus ibn Dizawayh ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Utba ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Uthman al-Awqas narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Abdur-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, I intended to order firewood to be gathered, then order the prayer and the call made for it, then order a man to lead the people in prayer, then go against men and burn their houses upon them with fire. By Him in whose Hand is my soul, had one of them known he would find a fat bone or two good trotters he would have attended Isha prayer. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Abu Uthman al-Awqas; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in it."
"4884","Abbad ibn Ali as-Sirini al-Jawhari, of the offspring of Khalid ibn Sirin, narrated to us, he said: Bakkar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah created Paradise, and created for it people with their clans and tribes; none is added to them nor decreased from them. And He created the Fire, and created for it people with their clans and tribes; none is added to them nor decreased from them. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, then for what do we act? He said: Act, for everyone is facilitated toward what he was created for. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Bakkar ibn Muhammad; Abbad ibn Ali is alone in it."
"4885","Abbad ibn Sa'id al-Ju'fi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Buhlul narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim Abu ad-Duha, from Masruq, from A'isha, who said: There was speech between me and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Shall I place Umar between me and you? I said: No. He said: Shall I place your father between me and you? I said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad."
"4886","Abbad ibn Sa'id al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Buhlul narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from Hashim ibn al-Barid, from Abu Sa'id at-Taymi, from Thabit, freedman of Abu Dharr, from Umm Salama, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Ali is with the Qur'an, and the Qur'an is with him; they will not part until they come to me at the Basin. This hadith is not narrated from Thabit, freedman of Abu Dharr, except with this chain; Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad is alone in it."
"4887","Abbad ibn Abdillah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ath-Thawri narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over an-Najashi and said takbir over him four times."
"4888","Ayyash ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Qatada, from Abdullah ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aqiqa is slaughtered on the seventh, or the fourteenth, or the twenty-first. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except Isma'il ibn Muslim."
"4889","Ayyash ibn Tamim as-Sukkari al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Sulayman ash-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the flesh of domestic donkeys. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Makhlad ibn Yazid."
"4890","Ayyash ibn Tamim narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Fazari, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda, from his father, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you passes in these markets with arrows, let him hold the blades. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda except Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Fazari; Muhammad ibn Salama is alone in it."
"4891","Ayyash ibn Tamim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: Kharija ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from A'isha, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Allah laughs at the despair and despondency of the servants, and the nearness of mercy to them. I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, does our Lord laugh? He said: Yes, by Him in whose Hand is my soul, He indeed laughs. I said: Then we will not be deprived of good when He laughs. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Kharija ibn Mus'ab; Salm ibn Salim is alone in it."
"4892","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This umma will split into seventy-three sects, all of them in the Fire except one. They said: What is that sect? He said: What I and my companions are upon today. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Abdullah ibn Sufyan."
"4893","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq informed us, from Sharik, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Muradi, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu al-Bakhtari at-Ta'i, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you belittle himself: when he sees a matter of Allah where he should speak, then Allah will say: What prevented you from speaking? He will say: I feared people. He will say: Me you were more entitled to fear. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Muradi except Sharik; Ishaq al-Azraq is alone in it."
"4894","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amrawayh al-Harawi narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Qatada, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man with a voluntary sacrificial animal that breaks down before reaching its place? He said: He slaughters it, then smears its sandal with its blood, then strikes its side with it, and does not eat from it; if he eats from it, its make-up becomes obligatory upon him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qatada except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Tahman is alone in it."
"4895","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amrawayh al-Harawi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Hassan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out to Makka, would bathe when he intended to enter ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan except Salih ibn Abi Hassan, nor from Salih except Khalid ibn Ilyas; Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid is alone in it."
"4896","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Thabit al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mahan ibn Abi Hanifa narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, who said: Two men disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I am only a man; I judge between you by what I hear from you, and perhaps one of you is more eloquent in his plea than his brother. Whoever I judge for him something of his brother's right, I only cut for him a piece of the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; al-Qasim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar is alone in it."
"4897","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Salih, from Amir ash-Sha'bi, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Samura, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fulfills the oaths of his parents, pays their debt, and does not cause them to be reviled, is recorded dutiful even if he was undutiful in their life; and whoever does not fulfill their oaths, pay their debt, and causes them to be reviled, is recorded undutiful even if he was dutiful in their life. This hadith is not narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Samura except with this chain; Ali ibn Sa'id al-Kindi is alone in it."
"4898","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Harun ibn Sa'd, from Abu as-Safar, from Hurra, from Asma bint Umays, who said: Ali proposed to me; that reached Fatima, so she mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: It is not for her to harm Allah and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Harun ibn Sa'd except Sulayman ibn Qarm; al-Jawhari is alone in it."
"4899","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Suhayl al-Warraq al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Muwarri' al-Anbari narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is clean, so cleanse yourselves; none enters Paradise except the clean."
"4900","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Suhayl al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Muwarri' al-Anbari narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a cup with milk and honey, and said: Two drinks in one drink? And two condiments in one cup? I have no need of it. Yet I do not claim it is unlawful; I dislike that Allah ask me about the luxuries of the world on the Day of Resurrection. Be humble toward Allah; whoever is humble toward Allah, Allah raises him; whoever is arrogant, Allah lowers him; whoever is moderate, Allah enriches him; and whoever remembers death much, Allah loves him. None narrated these two hadiths from Hisham ibn Urwa except Nu'aym ibn Muwarri'; Ahmad ibn Suhayl al-Warraq is alone in them."
"4901","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Suhayl al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Miswar ibn Muwarri' al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls for his ablution water, then when he finishes his ablution says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; O Allah, make me of the repentant and make me of the purified, eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; he enters by whichever he wishes. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Miswar ibn Muwarri'."
"4902","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A she-camel threw a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and killed him while he was in ihram. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bury him in his two garments, do not touch him with perfume, wash him with lote and water, do not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection saying labbayk. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Khalid."
"4903","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Suwayd ibn Ghafala, who said: We were on a journey of ours; we found a whip, and a man of the company took it. We forbade him but he refused. When we came to Madina we met Ubayy ibn Ka'b and mentioned that to him. He said: I found a hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I brought them to him. He said: Announce it a year. When the year came I brought them to him. He said: Announce it another year. I did; when the year came I brought them to him after three years. He said: Know its strap and its count, then enjoy it; if its seeker comes, give it to him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Khalid ibn Abdillah."
"4904","Isa ibn Muhammad as-Saydalani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uqba as-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Sinan al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Ka'b Abu Abdillah narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Know that Isa son of Maryam, there is no prophet nor messenger between me and him; know that he is my successor among my umma after me; know that he will kill the Dajjal, break the cross, and war will lay down its burdens. Know that whoever of you reaches him, let him convey salam to him. Abu Hurayra said: I hope to be the first to convey to him the salam of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and to eat from his bowl."
"4905","Amr ibn Thawr al-Judhami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: I seek protection for you two by the perfect words of Allah, from every devil and vermin, and from every harmful eye. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, except al-Firyabi. The well-known is: ath-Thawri, from Mansur, from al-Minhal."
"4906","Amr ibn Thawr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them enters Paradise. None narrated these two hadiths from Sufyan except al-Firyabi."
"4907","Amr ibn Thawr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Amr ibn Wahb, from al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, who said: I ended with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf; he stepped back, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him. We prayed what we caught and made up what we missed. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Firyabi."
"4908","Amr ibn Abi at-Tahir ibn as-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Nafi' ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulayka narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Basin is a month's journey, its corners equal, its spouts whiter than silver, its scent sweeter than musk, its cups like the stars of the sky. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulayka except Nafi' ibn Umar."
"4909","Amr ibn Abi at-Tahir ibn as-Sarh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Nafi' ibn Umar informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go for his need to al-Mughammas. Nafi' said: About two miles from Makka. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Nafi' ibn Umar; Ibn Abi Maryam is alone in it."
"4910","Amr ibn Abi at-Tahir ibn as-Sarh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Nafi' ibn Umar informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, walking, uncircumcised. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' ibn Umar except Ibn Abi Maryam."
"4911","Amr ibn Abi at-Tahir ibn as-Sarh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub az-Zam'i informed us, that Abu al-Huwayrith informed him, that Nu'aym ibn Abdillah al-Mujmir informed him, that Anas ibn Malik informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, whoever has them has tasted the flavor of faith: one to whom nothing is dearer than Allah and His Messenger; one to whom being burned with fire is dearer than reverting from his religion; and one who loves for Allah and hates for Allah. Nu'aym did not narrate any hadith from Anas except this one. He was called al-Mujmir because he used to perfume the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he is of the freedmen of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him. None narrated it from Abu al-Huwayrith except Musa; Ibn Abi Maryam is alone in it."
"4912","Amr ibn Hazim Abu al-Jahm ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd ar-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sulayman at-Taymi, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not fear of people prevent one of you from saying the truth when he sees or hears it. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman at-Taymi except Isa ibn Yunus."
"4913","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Rashid as-San'ani narrated to us, from Abu Asma ar-Rahabi, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be rulers over you who kill the prayers from their times; so pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them voluntary. When al-Hajjaj came he delayed the prayer from its times, so I would pray the prayer at its time and make my prayer with them voluntary. This hadith is not narrated from Shaddad ibn Aws except with this chain; Isma'il ibn Ayyash is alone in it."
"4914","Amr ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Bilal al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: I saw Abdullah ibn Busr, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sitting in the mosque, an old aged shaykh. His boy came to him and said: O my master, these camels of yours have been taken in the forced labor of az-Zibla, meaning the house of al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik at the door of the mosque at Hims. With him were two men; they took his upper arms until he stood. Umar said: I walked with him until he came to az-Zibla; his camels were kneeled, and they were shoveling dust with sacks. He took the sack and began opening for them. Some Christians said: This is your Prophet's companion; you do this with him? Had we seen a man of the companions of Isa we would have carried him upon our heads. The people moved to seize him, so he said: Leave me; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: How will you be when the rulers are unjust over you. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Busr except with this chain; Umar ibn Bilal is alone in it."
"4915","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Asbagh ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his grandfather Aban, from his father Sulayman, who said: The Islam of Qubath ibn Ashyam al-Laythi was that men of his people and others of the Arabs came to him and said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Muttalib has come out calling to a religion other than ours. Qubath stood until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he entered upon him he said to him: Sit, O Qubath. Qubath fell silent, or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you the one who says: Had the women of Quraysh come out with their cloaks they would have turned back Muhammad and his companions? Qubath said: By Him who sent you with the truth, my tongue did not move with it, my lips did not murmur with it, none heard it from me; it was only a thought that occurred in myself. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and that what you brought is truth. This hadith is not narrated from Qubath ibn Ashyam except with this chain; Asbagh ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Himsi is alone in it."
"4916","Amr ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Salim, from az-Zubaydi, he said: Isa ibn Yazid narrated to us, that Tawus Abu Abd ar-Rahman narrated to him, that Munabbih Abu Wahb narrated to him, tracing it to Mu'adh, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in a house of his wives' houses with A'isha beside him. Some Jews entered upon him and said: as-sam upon you, O Muhammad. He said: And upon you. They sat and spoke. A'isha understood the greeting with which they greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she gathered anger and endured, but could not hold her rage, and said: Rather upon you be as-sam, Allah's anger and His curse; with this do you greet the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Then they went out. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What carried you to what you said? She said: Did you not hear how they greeted you, O Messenger of Allah? By Allah, I could not hold myself when I heard their greeting to you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: No harm; how did you see me return upon them? The Jews are a people weary of their religion, an envious people; they did not envy the Muslims for anything better than three: returning salam, straightening rows, and their saying behind their imam in the prescribed prayer: Amin. This hadith is not narrated from Mu'adh ibn Jabal except with this chain, and we do not know Munabbih Abu Wahb to have narrated any hadith with a chain except this one."
"4917","Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Sulaym az-Zubaydi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: I found in the book of my grandfather Abd al-Jabbar ibn Sulaym az-Zubaydi: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him not dip anything into it until he washes it seven times. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Ibrahim ibn Muhammad; Isma'il ibn Ayyash is alone in it."
"4918","Amr ibn Ahmad al-Ammi an-Nahhas al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd az-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: My uncle narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Salama ibn Kuhayl al-Hadrami narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Burayda al-Aslami, from his father Burayda ibn al-Husayb, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves, so visit them, for their visit is admonition and lesson; I forbade you the flesh of sacrifices beyond three, so eat and store; and I forbade you nabidh in vessels, so drink, but do not drink unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Salama ibn Kuhayl except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd is alone in it, from his father."
"4919","Amr ibn Ahmad al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj ar-Riyashi narrated to us, he said: al-Asma'i narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, the Arabs apostatized, hypocrisy raised its head, and there befell my father what would have crushed mountains had it befallen them. By Allah, they did not differ in a point except my father flew with its share and spearhead. Then she mentions Ibn al-Khattab, saying: By Allah, he was keen-witted, unique, having prepared for matters their peers. Ar-Riyashi said: It is said of the outstanding man whom none resembles: unique; and it is said: lone wild ass; and it is said: lone colt. The poet said: turbaned in uniqueness. Ar-Riyashi said: Yasrandihi means: he overtops him. Al-Asma'i recited to us. No one narrated this hadith from al-Asma'i except ar-Riyashi."
"4920","Amr ibn Ahmad al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Abdillah al-Jazari al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Salih, from Asim ibn Abi Razin, that Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am old, blind, far from home, with no guide; do you find for me a concession? He said: Do you hear the call? He said: Yes. He said: I find no concession for you. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Salih ibn Hayy except Abdullah ibn Dawud."
"4921","Umara ibn Wathima ibn Musa ibn al-Furat al-Misri Abu Rifa'a narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, he said: Khalid ibn Abi Imran wrote to me, he said: Abu Ayyash narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdillah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Islam began strange, and it will return strange; so blessed are the strangers. He said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Those who set right when people corrupt."
"4922","Umara ibn Wathima narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, he said: Khalid ibn Abi Imran wrote to me, he said: Abu Ayyash narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no shepherd entrusted with a flock except he will be asked on the Day of Resurrection: Did he uphold Allah's command in it, or neglect it? None narrated these two hadiths from Yahya ibn Sa'id except al-Layth."
"4923","Umara ibn Wathima narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wives of the people of Paradise sing to their husbands with the finest voices anyone ever heard; of what they sing is; and of what they sing is. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Muhammad ibn Ja'far; Ibn Abi Maryam is alone in it."
"4924","Ghalib ibn Muhammad al-Barda'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Wara ar-Razi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ubaydullah ibn al-Wazi' narrated to us, from Ayyub as-Sakhtiyani, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, whoever does them trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is due upon Allah to aid him and bless him: whoever strives to free a neck trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is due upon Allah to aid him and bless him; whoever marries trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is due upon Allah to aid him and bless him; and whoever revives dead land trusting in Allah and seeking reward, it is due upon Allah to aid him and bless him."
"4925","Al-Fadl ibn Harun al-Baghdadi, companion of Abu Thawr, narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim at-Tarjuman narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Muslim al-Hamdani, from ash-Sha'bi, who said: Abu Hurayra saw a man and his appearance pleased him. He said: From whom are you? The man said: Of those upon whom Allah bestowed favor. He said: We are all of those upon whom Allah bestowed favor; from whom are you? He said: Of the people of the earth. He said: We are all of the people of the earth; from whom are you? He said: Of the Nabateans. He said: Move away from me; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Killers of the Prophets, and helpers of oppressors; when they take estates and build buildings, then flee, flee. No one narrated this hadith from ash-Sha'bi except Sa'id ibn Muslim al-Hamdani; Abdur-Rahman ibn Malik ibn Mighwal is alone in it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"4926","Al-Fadl ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim at-Tarjuman narrated to us, he said: Abd ar-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi narrated to us, from his father, from Urwa ibn az-Zubayr, from A'isha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the Qur'an in whatever reading, Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases ten evil deeds from him, and raises him ten degrees. Whoever recites, parsing some and erring in some, twenty good deeds are written for him, twenty evil deeds erased from him, and he is raised twenty degrees. Whoever recites, parsing all of it, forty good deeds are written for him, forty evil deeds erased from him, and he is raised forty degrees. No one narrated this hadith from Urwa except Zayd al-Ammi; Abd ar-Rahim ibn Zayd is alone in it."
"4927","Al-Fadl ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim at-Tarjuman narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Haritha ibn Muhammad, from Amra, from A'isha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath involving severance, its expiation is not to persist upon it. No one narrated this hadith from Haritha except Hibban ibn Ali, and it is not narrated from A'isha except with this chain."
"4928","Al-Fadl ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid ar-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: My father Umar ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Musa ibn A'yan, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from az-Zuhri, he said: Urwa informed me, that A'isha informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to encourage people to stand in Ramadan without commanding them with a decisive command in it, saying: Whoever stands Ramadan in faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away with the matter upon that; the matter was upon that in the caliphate of Abu Bakr and the early part of Umar's caliphate. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Rashid except Musa ibn A'yan."
"4929","Al-Fadl ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from as-Suddi, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, regarding His saying: You are only a warner, and for every people a guide. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The warner, and the guide: a man of Banu Hashim. No one narrated this hadith from as-Suddi except al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad; Uthman ibn Abi Shayba is alone in it."
"4930","Al-Fadl ibn Abi Rawh al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Ubayda ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Ukli, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid an-Nakha'i, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the traveler three, and for the resident a day and a night, wiping over the leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith al-Ukli except al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, nor from al-Qasim except Ubayda; Abdullah ibn Umar is alone in it."
"4931","4925 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Abi Rawh, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban, he said: Narrated to us Yahya ibn Hammad at-Ta'i, he said: Narrated to us Ismah ibn Zamil, from his father, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said to those around him from his ummah: ""Guarantee for me six traits and I will guarantee Paradise for you."" I said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""The prayer, the zakah, the trust, the private part, the stomach, and the tongue."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Abdullah ibn Umar alone transmitted it."
"4932","4926 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas al-Qirtimi al-Baghdadi, he said: Narrated to us Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar, he said: Narrated to us Amr ibn Abd al-Jabbar, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Adam, he said: Narrated to me Anas ibn Malik, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me things I will not abandon until I die: he enjoined upon me the two rak'ahs of Fajr, he said: ""In them are the precious things of the age,"" and the two rak'ahs of Duha, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning, and two rak'ahs before Zuhr and two after it, and two before Asr, and two after Maghrib, and two after Isha, and fasting three days of every month, he said: ""It is the fast of the age,"" and that I not spend a night except upon witr. And he said to me: ""O Abu Hurayrah, pray two rak'ahs at the beginning of the day and I guarantee for you its end."" This hadith is not narrated from Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, except with this chain; Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar alone transmitted it."
"4933","4927 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas, he said: Narrated to us Ismail ibn Isa al-Attar, he said: Narrated to us Amr ibn Abd al-Jabbar, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Yazid ibn Adam, from Abu ad-Darda and Abu Umamah and Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' and Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah loves that His concessions be accepted, just as the servant loves the forgiveness of his Lord."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu ad-Darda, Abu Umamah, Wathilah and Anas except with this chain; Ismail ibn Isa alone transmitted it."
"4934","4928 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas, he said: Narrated to us Yahya ibn Uthman al-Harbi, he said: Narrated to us Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar and his brother Abdullah ibn Umar and Musa ibn Uqbah and Abdullah ibn Ziyad ibn Sam'an and Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah and Burd ibn Sinan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment toward Najd, I was in it, and our shares reached twelve, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us an extra camel each. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah except by Ismail ibn Ayyash."
"4935","4929 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani, he said: Narrated to us Bashshar ibn Musa al-Khaffaf, he said: Narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Awwam, he said: Narrated to us Sufyan ibn Husayn, from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The foot is barren (jubbar, i.e. no liability)."" This hadith was not narrated from az-Zuhri except by Sufyan ibn Husayn."
"4936","4930 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas, he said: Narrated to us Bashshar ibn Musa al-Khaffaf, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani, he said: Narrated to us al-Awza'i, from Rabi'ah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will emerge from the Jewry of Asbahan, and with him seventy thousand Jews, upon them the sijan (cloaks)."" This hadith was not narrated from al-Awza'i, from Rabi'ah, except by Muhammad ibn Mus'ab."
"4937","4931 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Ja'far al-Misri, he said: Narrated to us al-Musayyib ibn Wadih, he said: Narrated to us Ali ibn Bakkar, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The people of kindness in this world are the people of kindness in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter."" This hadith was not narrated from Hisham ibn Hassan except by Ali ibn Bakkar; al-Musayyib ibn Wadih alone transmitted it."
"4938","4932 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn ar-Rabi' al-Kindi al-Ladhiqi, he said: Narrated to us Abd al-Wahid ibn Shu'ayb al-Jabali at Jabalah, he said: Narrated to us Salamah ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: Narrated to us Salamah ibn Kalthum, from al-Awza'i, from Qurrah, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that a man was admonishing his brother regarding modesty, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Leave him, for modesty is part of faith."" This hadith was not narrated from al-Awza'i except by Salamah ibn Kalthum; Salamah ibn Abd al-Aziz alone transmitted it."
"4939","4933 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani al-Burzabadhani, he said: Narrated to us Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali, he said: Narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity."" This hadith was not narrated from Mujahid except by Layth, nor from Layth except by Hafs; Ismail ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"4940","4934 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Salih ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Ja'far al-Mansur al-Hashimi, he said: Narrated to us Hudbah ibn Khalid, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani, he said: Narrated to us Abbad ibn Mansur, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, he said: Narrated to me Abu Qu'ays that he came to A'ishah and sought permission to enter upon her, and she disliked giving him permission. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, she said: O Prophet of Allah, Abu Qu'ays came to me and I refused to permit him. He said: ""Let your paternal uncle enter upon you."" And Abu Qu'ays was the brother of A'ishah's foster-mother. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qu'ays except with this chain, and Abu Qu'ays narrated no hadith other than this one."
"4941","4935 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Salih al-Hashimi, he said: Narrated to us as-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari, he said: Narrated to us Amr ibn Hamzah ibn Usayd, he said: Narrated to us Khalaf, meaning ad-Dabbi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Glory be to Allah, what has come upon you, and what are you facing?"" three times. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Has revelation come down, or has a promised event arrived? He said: ""Indeed Allah forgives on the first night of the month of Ramadan every people of this qiblah."" A man before him, shaking his head, said: Bakh, bakh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""As if your chest grew tight?"" He said: No, but I remembered the hypocrite. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The hypocrite is a disbeliever, and the disbeliever has no share in that."" This hadith is not narrated from Anas ibn Malik except with this chain; Amr ibn Hamzah alone transmitted it."
"4942","4936 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi, he said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, he said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Sadaqah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, in marfu' form, he said: He said [...]: ""Cast half of me into the sea and half of me onto the land."" He said: So He summoned the sea with what was in it and the land with what was in it, and said: ""What carried you to do what you did?"" He said: O my Lord, fear of You. He said: And nothing met him but it (i.e. it sufficed him). This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Sadaqah except by Hammad ibn Zayd, nor from Hammad except by al-Hajabi."
"4943","4937 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Amr ibn Marzuq, he said: Narrated to us Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding Laylat al-Qadr, that it is the night of the twenty-seventh or twenty-ninth, and that the angels on that night on earth are more numerous than the number of pebbles. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah except by Imran al-Qattan."
"4944","4938 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath, he said: Narrated to us ar-Rabi' ibn Badr, he said: Narrated to us Harun ibn Ri'ab al-Usaydi, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The fragrance of Paradise is scented from a journey of five hundred years, and the one who reminds others of his deeds, the disobedient to parents, and the habitual drinker of wine will not find its scent."" This hadith was not narrated from Harun ibn Ri'ab except by ar-Rabi' ibn Badr."
"4945","4939 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abu al-Walid, he said: Narrated to us Ghawth ibn Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Misri, he said: Narrated to me my father Sulayman ibn Ziyad, he said: We entered upon Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz' az-Zubaydi on a Friday, and he called for a basin and urinated in it, and said to the slave girl: Shield me, so she shielded him. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding that one of you urinate facing the qiblah. This hadith was not narrated from Ghawth ibn Sulayman except by Abu al-Walid."
"4946","4940 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi, he said: Khallad ibn Qurrah ibn Khalid mentioned, from his father, he said: Narrated to us al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, he said: We were at al-Mirbad, and a Bedouin came to us with a piece of leather, and said: See what is in it, and behold a letter from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Banu Zuhayr ibn Uqaysh, a clan of Ukl: ""If you establish the prayer, give the zakah, pay a fifth of what you gain as spoils, and the share of the Prophet and the safi (select portion), then you are secure with the security of Allah."" I said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard him say: ""Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month remove the rancor of the chest."" We said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I see you suspect me; so he took the sheet and went away. We asked about him, and it was said: This is an-Namir ibn Tawlab al-Ukli. This hadith was not narrated from Khallad ibn Qurrah except by Muhammad ibn Sallam."
"4947","4941 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Jumahi, he said: Narrated to us Abd al-Wahhab ath-Thaqafi, from Anbasah al-Ghanawi, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened in killing until their killing reached the children, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."" This hadith was not narrated from Anbasah al-Ghanawi except by Abd al-Wahhab ath-Thaqafi; Muhammad ibn Sallam alone transmitted it."
"4948","4942 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Harb, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abi Razin, he said: Narrated to me my mother, she said: Umm al-Harir, when a man of the Arabs died, would grieve intensely over him. It was said to her: Umm al-Harir, why do we see you grieve intensely when a man of the Arabs dies? She said: I heard my master say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Among the approach of the Hour is the destruction of the Arabs."" Muhammad said: And her master is Talhah ibn Malik."
"4949","4943 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, he said: Narrated to us Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashja'i, he said: Narrated to us al-Harith ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Sulayman ibn Yasar and Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""For what the sky and springs water, a tenth; and for what is watered by drawing (camels), half a tenth."" This hadith was not narrated from Sulayman ibn Yasar and Busr ibn Sa'id except by al-Harith ibn Abd ar-Rahman."
"4950","4944 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi, he said: Narrated to us Hisham Abu al-Miqdam, from his mother, from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is struck by a calamity and then, when he remembers it, says: Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we return, Allah renews for him a reward for it like what it was on the day it struck him."" This hadith is not narrated from al-Husayn ibn Ali except with this chain; Abu al-Miqdam alone transmitted it."
"4951","4945 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Ali ibn al-Madini, he said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq, he said: Narrated to us Hallam ibn Salih, he said: Narrated to me Salim ibn Rabi'ah al-Absi, from Hudhayfah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bought a slave, what shall I do with him? He said: ""Your brother in Islam; feed him from what you eat, clothe him from what you wear, and if you dislike him, sell him."" This hadith is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain; Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Warraq alone transmitted it."
"4952","4946 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abu al-Walid at-Tayalisi, he said: Narrated to us al-Aswad ibn Shayban, from Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like the comprehensive supplications and leave what is besides that. This hadith is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain; al-Aswad ibn Shayban alone transmitted it."
"4953","4947 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abu al-Walid, he said: Narrated to us Ikrimah ibn Ammar, he said: Narrated to me Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from his uncle Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque, and a Bedouin entered and sat urinating. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mah, mah (stop, stop). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not cut him off,"" then he called him and said: ""These mosques are not suitable for anything of filth [...], or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said; they are only for recitation of the Qur'an, prayer, and remembrance of Allah."" Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over it. This hadith was not narrated from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah except by Ikrimah ibn Ammar and Hammam ibn Yahya."
"4954","4948 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi, he said: Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Abu Ishaq, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever I am mentioned in his presence, let him send blessings upon me, for whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah sends blessings upon him tenfold."" This hadith was not narrated from Abu Ishaq except by Ibrahim ibn Tahman; Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sallam alone transmitted it."
"4955","4949 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sallam, he said: Narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he allotted houses, and he allotted to Ibn Mas'ud among those he allotted. His companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, set him apart from us. He said: ""Then for what did Allah send me? Indeed Allah does not sanctify a nation in which the weak among them are not given their right."" This hadith was not narrated from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, well-mastered, except by Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sallam."
"4956","4950 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Shadh ibn al-Fayyad, he said: Narrated to us Abu Qahdham, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar passed by Mu'adh ibn Jabal while he was weeping, and said: What makes you weep? He said: A hadith I heard from the occupant of this grave, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed the least of showing-off is shirk, and the most beloved servants to Allah are the pious, the hidden, who when absent are not missed, and when present are not known; those are the guides of guidance and the lamps of knowledge."" This hadith was not narrated from Abu Qilabah except by Abu Qahdham, whose name is an-Nadr ibn Ma'bad al-Jarmi."
"4957","4951 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak, he said: Narrated to us Bazi' Abu al-Khalil, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in the spot where al-Hasan and al-Husayn urinate, and said: ""Indeed when the servant prostrates to Allah a prostration, Allah purifies the place of his prostration to seven earths."""
"4958","4952 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak, he said: Narrated to us Bazi' Abu al-Khalil, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Dissolve your food with remembrance of Allah and prayer, and do not sleep upon it lest your hearts harden."" These two hadiths were not narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah except by Bazi' Abu al-Khalil."
"4959","4953 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Shadh ibn al-Fayyad, he said: Narrated to us Hashim ibn Sa'id, he said: Narrated to me Kinanah, from Safiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed me and made my freedom my dowry. This hadith is not narrated from Safiyyah except with this chain."
"4960","4954 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Shadh ibn al-Fayyad, he said: Narrated to us Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise."" This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah except by Umar ibn Ibrahim; Shadh alone transmitted it."
"4961","4955 - Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab, he said: Narrated to us Abu Ma'mar al-Muqa'id, he said: Narrated to us Abd al-Warith, he said: Narrated to us Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from A'ishah, she said: When there was revealed: ""Among which are verses precise, they are the foundation of the Book, and others unspecific; as for those in whose hearts is deviation, they follow what is unspecific of it, seeking discord and seeking its interpretation,"" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you see the disputants who dispute concerning it, then they are they."" This hadith was not narrated from Ali ibn Zayd except by Abd al-Warith."
"4962","4956 - Of those named Fudayl: Narrated to us Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati, he said: Narrated to us Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, he said: Narrated to us Zayd ibn Hibban ar-Raqqi, from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he used to forbid the fasting person from kissing, and would say: ""None of you has of protection what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had."" This hadith was not narrated from az-Zuhri except by Zayd ibn Hibban."
"4963","4957 - Narrated to us Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati, he said: Narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, he said: Narrated to us Abu ad-Daws, he said: A man called Abu Ma'qil came to me and said to me: Write; so he wrote: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. He said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: My close friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me fasting three days of every month, sleeping upon witr, and the glorification of Duha."
"4964","4958 - Narrated to us Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati, he said: Narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, he said: Narrated to us Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed Dhu al-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Syria, Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and Qarn for the people of Ta'if. This hadith was not narrated from Maymun ibn Mihran except by Ja'far ibn Burqan."
"4965","4959 - Narrated to us Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati, he said: Narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, he said: Narrated to us Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn Suhayb al-Faqir, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the jar, the varnished, the gourd, and the hollowed stump. This hadith was not narrated from Yazid al-Faqir except by Ja'far ibn Burqan."
"4966","4960 - Narrated to us Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati, he said: Narrated to us Abu Nu'aym, he said: Narrated to us Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Arafah ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed Dhu al-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Syria, Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and Qarn for the people of Ta'if. Then he said: ""These are for their people and for others who pass through them besides their people."" This hadith was not narrated from Ja'far ibn Burqan except by Abu Nu'aym."
"4967","4961 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Afaf ibn Sulaym al-Fawzi al-Himsi, he said: Narrated to us my uncle Ahmad ibn Muslim, he said: Narrated to us Isa ibn Yunus, from Zakariyya, from ash-Sha'bi, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Hudhayfah, he said: I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came to a rubbish-heap of a people and urinated standing, then called me and said: ""Why did you step aside?"" So I came until I was at his heels, then water was brought and he performed ablution and wiped over the two khuffs. This hadith was not narrated from ash-Sha'bi except by Zakariyya, nor from Zakariyya except by Isa ibn Yunus; Ahmad ibn Sulaym al-Fawzi alone transmitted it."
"4968","4962 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn al-Layth Abu Salih ar-Rasibi, he said: Narrated to us al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from Sa'id ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed wine, and cursed its pourer, its drinker, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the eater of its price. This hadith was not narrated from Abdullah ibn Abdullah except by Sa'id ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Wa'il; Fulayh alone transmitted it."
"4969","4963 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn al-Layth ar-Rasibi, he said: Narrated to us al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from Khawwat ibn Salih ibn Khawwat, from his paternal aunt Umm Amr bint Khawwat, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who joins hair and the one who asks for it to be joined. This hadith was not narrated from Umm Amr bint Khawwat except by Khawwat ibn Salih; Fulayh alone transmitted it."
"4970","4964 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn al-Layth ar-Rasibi, he said: Narrated to us al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: Suwayd ibn Ghafalah informed me, he said: I went out, I and Zayd ibn Suhan and Salman ibn Rabi'ah, and I picked up a whip, and he ordered me to leave it but I refused. When we came to Madinah I mentioned that to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and he said: You did right; I picked up one hundred dinars at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it, and he ordered me to announce it for a year, then I informed him it was not recognized, then he ordered me to announce it, so I announced it a year, then I informed him it was not recognized, then he ordered me to announce it, so I announced it a year, then I informed him it was not recognized, and he said: ""Know its container and its tie, then fulfill your need with it, and if a seeker comes for it, return it."" This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except by Fulayh; al-Mu'afa alone transmitted it."
"4971","4965 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn al-Layth, he said: Narrated to us al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Fulayh, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once led us in prayer, then ascended the minbar, and gestured with his hand toward the qiblah of prayer. When he finished he said: ""Just now, since I prayed for you, I have seen Paradise and Hell before this wall, and I have not seen like today in good and evil,"" three times."
"4972","4966 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn al-Layth, he said: Narrated to us al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and said: ""I see you behind me as I see you in front of me."" These two hadiths were not narrated from Hilal ibn Ali except by Fulayh ibn Sulayman."
"4973","4967 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ad-Dallal al-Kufi, he said: Narrated to us Mikhwal ibn Ibrahim, he said: Narrated to us Isra'il, from Mansur, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""I was sent, I and the Hour, like these two."" This hadith was not narrated from Mansur except by Isra'il."
"4974","4968 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ad-Dallal, he said: Narrated to us Shihab ibn Abbad, he said: Narrated to us Mindal ibn Ali, from Sulayman at-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened before a cat lest it pass in front of him in prayer. This hadith was not narrated from Sulayman at-Taymi except by Mindal."
"4975","4969 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ad-Dallal, he said: Narrated to us Usayd ibn Zayd al-Jammal, he said: Narrated to us Qays ibn ar-Rabi', from Layth, from Ata, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The gifts of rulers are misappropriation (ghulul)."" This hadith was not narrated from Ata except by Layth; Qays alone transmitted it."
"4976","4970 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi al-Ikhmimi al-Misri, he said: Narrated to us my uncle Muhammad ibn Mahdi, he said: Narrated to us Yazid ibn Yunus ibn Yazid, from his father Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Narrated to me Abu Idris al-Khawlani that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution, let him blow his nose, and whoever cleans with stones, let him do so an odd number of times."""
"4977","4971 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi, he said: Narrated to us my uncle Muhammad ibn Mahdi, he said: Narrated to us Yazid ibn Yunus ibn Yazid, from his father, from az-Zuhri, he said: Narrated to me Abu Salamah that A'ishah narrated to him, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to sleep while junub, he would perform his ablution for prayer."
"4978","4972 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi, he said: Narrated to us my uncle Muhammad ibn Mahdi, he said: Narrated to us Yazid ibn Yunus ibn Yazid, from his father, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi informed me that Humran, freedman of Uthman, informed him that Uthman performed ablution three times three times, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution like my ablution, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution like this ablution of mine, then bows two rak'ahs, not speaking to himself in them except of good, is forgiven what preceded of his sin."" This hadith was not narrated from Yazid ibn Yunus except by Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-Ikhmimi."
"4979","4973 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi, he said: Narrated to us Abu Mutarrif al-Mughirah ibn Mutarrif al-Wasiti, he said: Narrated to us Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from Mu'awiyah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of Ashura and said: ""This is a day whose fasting was not prescribed for you, and I am fasting; so whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may break fast."" This hadith was not narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah except by Abu al-Mutarrif; Bishr ibn Mu'adh alone transmitted it."
"4980","4974 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn Mu'adh, he said: Narrated to us Zuhayr ibn Ishaq, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: I ate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and Umar, bread and meat, then they prayed and did not perform ablution. This hadith was not narrated from Yunus except by Zuhayr ibn Ishaq; Bishr ibn Mu'adh alone transmitted it."
"4981","4975 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn ar-Rabi' ibn Sulayman al-Basri, he said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd ar-Rahman, from Abu Qatadah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The (good) dream is from Allah, and the nightmare is from Satan; so when one of you sees what he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge, for it will not harm him."" This hadith was not narrated from Ayyub except by Hammad ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn ar-Rabi' ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"4982","4976 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami, he said: Narrated to us my father, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: You saw us on the day of Hunayn, with both parties indeed turning away, and there were not with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hundred men. This hadith was not narrated from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except by Sufyan ibn Husayn, nor from Sufyan except by Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami; his son Muhammad alone transmitted it."
"4983","4977 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Yusuf as-Sayrafi, he said: Narrated to us Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Perform Hajj and Umrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows remove the dross of iron."" This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Aqil except by Yazid, nor from Yazid except by Abu Bakr; Ibrahim ibn Yusuf alone transmitted it."
"4984","4978 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn as-Sabbah al-Jarjarai, he said: Narrated to us Ata ibn Jabalah, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: I came from a journey and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""When you come to your family, do a prudent deed."" So I came to my family and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you come to your family, do a prudent deed."" She said to me: Here you are. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Ata ibn Jabalah; Muhammad ibn as-Sabbah alone transmitted it."
"4985","4979 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Yusuf as-Sayrafi, he said: Narrated to us Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from his brother Sa'd ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the age."" Hafs said: Then I met Sa'd and he narrated it to me. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from his brother, except by Hafs; Ibrahim ibn Yusuf alone transmitted it."
"4986","4980 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman Abu Yahya Sa'iqah, he said: Narrated to us Sadaqah ibn Sabiq, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Allah did not send a prophet to a people and take him except that He made after him a gap (fatrah), and Hell is filled from that gap."" This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except by Abu az-Zubayr, nor from Abu az-Zubayr except by Sulayman ibn Qarm; Sadaqah ibn Sabiq alone transmitted it."
"4987","4981 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us al-Walid ibn Shuja' as-Sakuni, he said: Narrated to us al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab, from Ma'qil ibn Ubaydullah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws and his legs, I guarantee for him Paradise."" This hadith was not narrated from Amr ibn Dinar except by Ma'qil ibn Ubaydullah, nor from Ma'qil except by al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab; al-Walid ibn Shuja' alone transmitted it."
"4988","4982 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Ali ibn Shu'ayb as-Simsar, he said: Narrated to us Ali ibn Asim, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake junub from other than wet dream, then bathe, then fast that day. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id except by Ali ibn Asim; Ali ibn Shu'ayb alone transmitted it."
"4989","4983 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Abd ar-Rahim ibn Muhammad as-Sukkari gave me a book, and I wrote from it: Narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Awwam, he said: Narrated to us Aban ibn Taghlib, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis."""
"4990","4984 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Abd ar-Rahim ibn Muhammad as-Sukkari gave me a book, and I wrote from it: Narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Awwam, he said: Narrated to us Aban ibn Taghlib, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever makes people hear of his deed, Allah will make the hearers of His creation hear of him on the Day of Resurrection, and belittle him and make him small."""
"4991","4985 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Abd ar-Rahim ibn Muhammad as-Sukkari gave me a book, and I wrote from it: Narrated to us Abbad ibn al-Awwam, he said: Narrated to us Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Musayyib ibn Abd Khayr, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr at the beginning of the night and its middle, then settled it at its end. These three hadiths were not narrated from Aban ibn Taghlib except by Abbad ibn al-Awwam; Abd ar-Rahim ibn Muhammad as-Sukkari alone transmitted them."
"4992","4986 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Halim an-Naysaburi, he said: Narrated to us Mubashshir ibn Abdullah, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding His saying: ""Indeed We suffice you against the mockers,"" and he said: The mockers are al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth, al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib Abu Zam'ah of Banu Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza, al-Harith ibn Ghayt al-Sahmi, and al-As ibn Wa'il as-Sahmi. Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained of them to him, and he showed him Abu Amr al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, and Jibril gestured to his ankle-vein (abjal), and he said: What did you do? He said: I have sufficed you against him. Then he showed him al-Harith ibn Ghaytal as-Sahmi, and he gestured to his belly, and he said: What did you do? He said: I have sufficed you against him. Then he showed him al-As ibn Wa'il as-Sahmi, and he gestured to the sole of his foot, and he said: What did you do? He said: I have sufficed you against him. As for al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, a man of Khuza'ah passed by him while feathering his arrows, and it struck his ankle-vein and severed it. As for al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib, he went blind; some say he went blind thus, and some say he alighted under a tree and kept saying: O my sons, will you not defend me? I am perishing, pierced by thorns in my eye, and they kept saying: We see nothing, and he remained so until his eyes went blind. As for al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth, sores broke out on his head and he died of them. As for al-Harith ibn Ghaytal, yellow water seized him in his belly until his excrement came out of his mouth, and he died of it. As for al-As ibn Wa'il, while he was thus one day, a thorn-bush (shibriqah) entered his foot until it filled from it, and he died. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Bishr Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah except by Sufyan ibn Husayn; Mubashshir ibn Abdullah alone transmitted it."
"4993","4987 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Halim, he said: Narrated to us Mubashshir ibn Abdullah, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Humayd at-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The prayer came while among the people were those not in ablution, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a basin, placed his hand in it, and water began gushing from between his fingers until they all performed ablution, and we were nearly eighty. This hadith was not narrated from Sufyan ibn Husayn except by Mubashshir ibn Abdullah."
"4994","4988 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Warith al-Warraq al-Baghdadi, he said: Narrated to us Abu ar-Rabi' az-Zahrani, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Ward, from al-Hasan ibn Jubayr, or Kathir, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of a third, for that hurts the believer, and Allah dislikes hurting the believer."" This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Ibn al-Mubarak alone transmitted it."
"4995","4989 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Warith, he said: Narrated to us Abu ar-Rabi' az-Zahrani, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, he said: Narrated to me my father, from Thumamah, from Anas, he said: In the ring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were three lines: Muhammad one line, and ""Messenger"" one line, and ""Allah"" one line. This hadith was not narrated from Thumamah except by Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna; Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari alone transmitted it."
"4996","4990 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Warith, he said: Narrated to us Abu ar-Rabi' az-Zahrani, he said: Narrated to us Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Take sahur, for in sahur is blessing."" This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman except by Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad; Abu ar-Rabi' alone transmitted it."
"4997","4991 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Warith, he said: Narrated to us Abu ar-Rabi' az-Zahrani, he said: Narrated to us Abu Hafs al-Abbar, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Uthman ibn Affan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Isha prayer in congregation equals standing a night, and the Fajr prayer in congregation equals standing a night."" This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id except by Abu Hafs al-Abbar; Abu ar-Rabi' alone transmitted it."
"4998","4992 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Warith, he said: Narrated to us Abu ar-Rabi' az-Zahrani, he said: Narrated to us Abu Ma'shar, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever covers a shame of his brother, it is as if he gave life to a buried girl."" This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except by Abu Ma'shar; Abu ar-Rabi' alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"4999","4993 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi, he said: Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari, he said: Narrated to us Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil, he said: Narrated to us Anbasah ibn Mihran al-Haddad, he said: Narrated to us az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best warriors in the path of Allah are their servant, then the one who brings them news, and the most special of them in rank with Allah is the fasting one; and whoever draws water for his companions a skin in the path of Allah outruns them to Paradise by seventy degrees or seventy years."""
"5000","4994 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abbad, he said: Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Buhlul, he said: Narrated to us Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil, from Anbasah al-Haddad, from az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah admits to Paradise through a single arrow three: its maker seeking reward for its making, the one who supplies it, and the one who shoots it."" These two hadiths were not narrated from az-Zuhri except by Anbasah al-Haddad; Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil alone transmitted them."
"5001","4995 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abbad, he said: Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Buhlul, he said: Narrated to us Salim ibn Nuh, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah has pardoned for my ummah what their souls speak of, so long as they do not act on it or speak of it."" This hadith was not narrated from Yunus ibn Ubayd except by Salim ibn Nuh."
"5002","4996 - Narrated to us al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi, he said: Narrated to us Hashim ibn al-Walid al-Harawi, he said: Narrated to us Waki' ibn al-Jarrah, from Umar ibn Husayl ibn Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: I heard ash-Sha'bi say: Dihyah ibn Khalifah al-Kalbi said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not cross for you a donkey upon a mare, so it produces for you a mule to ride? He said: ""Only those who do not know do that."" This hadith was not narrated from Dihyah except by ash-Sha'bi, nor from ash-Sha'bi except by Umar ibn Husayl; Waki' alone transmitted it."
"5003","4997 - Narrated to us Abu al-Fadl al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Birti at Baghdad, he said: Narrated to us Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Zurarah ar-Raqqi, he said: Narrated to us Ya'la ibn al-Ashdaq, he said: I heard my uncle Abdullah ibn Jarad say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Perform Hajj, for Hajj washes sins as water washes dirt."""
"5004","4998 - Of those named Qays: Narrated to us Qays ibn Abi Qays al-Bukhari, he said: Narrated to us Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi, he said: Narrated to us al-Fadl ibn Musa as-Sinani, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""O Ali, shall I not teach you a supplication which, when you supplicate with it, you are forgiven, even if you are already forgiven?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Most Great; there is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Most Generous; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne."" This hadith was not narrated from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, except by al-Husayn ibn Waqid. And Ali ibn Salih ibn Hayy narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali. And Isra'il narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali."
"5005","4999 - Narrated to us Qays ibn Muslim al-Bukhari, he said: Narrated to us Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi, he said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Amr an-Nasibi, from Hamzah ibn Abi Hamzah an-Nasibi, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: It was said to him: You have praised Abdullah ibn Mas'ud well? He said: What prevents me from that, when I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Read the Qur'an from four: from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Salim freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and Mu'adh ibn Jabal""? Then he said: ""I intended to send them to the nations as Isa sent the disciples."" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not send Abu Bakr and Umar, for they are better? He said: ""I cannot do without them; they are to this religion as hearing and sight are to the head."" This hadith was not narrated from Nafi' except by Hamzah ibn Abi Hamzah."
"5006","5000 - Narrated to us Qays ibn Muslim al-Bukhari, he said: Narrated to us Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, he said: Narrated to us Ma'n ibn Isa al-Qazzaz, he said: Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah, from his uncle Musa ibn Talhah, he said: I entered upon Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, and when I came out he called me, he said: Shall I place with you a hadith, O son of my brother, which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Then he said: I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Talhah is among those who fulfilled their vow,"" meaning what he pledged. This hadith is not narrated from Mu'awiyah except with this chain; Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah alone transmitted it."
"5007","5001 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib, that Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to him, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""When Allah loves a servant, He says to Jibril: I love My servant so-and-so, so love him; so Jibril loves him, and says to the inhabitants of heaven: Allah loves His servant so-and-so, so love him; so the inhabitants of heaven love him, and acceptance is placed for him in the earth."" This hadith was not narrated from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib except by Zuhayr."
"5008","5002 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, he said: Narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from A'ishah, that she bought Barirah from a man of the Ansar and they stipulated the wala'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The wala' belongs to the one who confers the favor."" He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice, and her husband was a slave, and she gifted meat to A'ishah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you not make for us from this meat? A'ishah said: It was given in charity to Barirah. He said: ""It is charity for her and a gift for us."" This hadith was not narrated from Simak ibn Harb except by Za'idah."
"5009","5003 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, he said: Narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, he said: Narrated to us Ammar ibn Abi Mu'awiyah al-Bajali, from Abu Salamah, he said: Narrated to me Umm Salamah that she used to bathe with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from janabah from a single vessel. This hadith was not narrated from Simak ibn Harb except by Za'idah; Mu'awiyah ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"5010","5004 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, he said: Narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr at Makkah, two rak'ahs, the prayer of the traveler. This hadith was not narrated from Simak ibn Harb except by Za'idah; Mu'awiyah ibn Amr alone transmitted it."
"5011","5005 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, and said: ""Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer."" A'ishah said: Abu Bakr is a tender-hearted man. He said: ""Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are the companions of Yusuf."" He said: Abu Bakr stood (leading) in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except by Za'idah."
"5012","5006 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, he said: Narrated to us Sufyan ibn Sa'id ath-Thawri, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Ata ibn Mina, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We prostrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in ""When the sky splits"" and ""Read in the name of your Lord."""
"5013","5007 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, he said: Narrated to us Sufyan ibn Sa'id, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah to Makkah, praying two rak'ahs two rak'ahs until he returned; and we stayed at Makkah ten (days), shortening therein until he returned."
"5014","5008 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, he said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Mikhwal, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Friday prayer Surah al-Jumu'ah and Surah al-Munafiqun."
"5015","5009 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, he said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, he said: Witr is not obligatory, but it is a sunnah which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established."
"5016","5010 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Umar, he said: The prayer of Adha is two rak'ahs, the prayer of Fitr is two rak'ahs, the Friday prayer is two rak'ahs, and the traveler's prayer is two rak'ahs, complete, not shortened, upon the tongue of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5017","5011 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, from Sufyan, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir over an-Najashi four times."
"5018","5012 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, from Sufyan, from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, regarding a daughter, a son's daughter, and a sister, he said: But I judge with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged: to the daughter a half, to the son's daughter a sixth completing two-thirds, and what remains to the full sister."
"5019","5013 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us Za'idah, from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Muhammad ibn Muslim az-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The Muslim does not inherit the mushrik, nor the mushrik the Muslim."" These hadiths were not narrated from Za'idah except by Mu'awiyah ibn Amr and Husayn al-Ju'fi."
"5020","5014 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail an-Nahdi, he said: Narrated to us Zuhayr, he said: Narrated to us Utbah ibn Humayd ad-Dabbi, he said: Narrated to us Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not go out on the day of Fitr until he ate dates, three, or five, or seven, or fewer than that or more, odd. This hadith was not narrated from Utbah ibn Humayd except by Zuhayr; Abu Ghassan alone transmitted it."
"5021","5015 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail, he said: Narrated to us Asbat ibn Nasr, from as-Suddi, from Subayh, freedman of Umm Salamah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to Ali, Fatimah, Hasan and Husayn: ""I am at war with whomever you war against, at peace with whomever you are at peace with."" This hadith was not narrated from as-Suddi except by Asbat ibn Nasr."
"5022","5016 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Abu Ghassan, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bishr, he said: Narrated to us Hani ibn Uthman, Abu Uthman ibn Hani, from his mother Humaydah bint Yasir, from her grandmother Yusayrah, and she was one of the migrant women, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O believing women, hold to tahlil, tasbih and taqdis, and count with the fingertips, for they will be questioned and asked to speak; and do not be heedless lest you forget mercy."" This hadith is not narrated from Yusayrah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Bishr alone transmitted it."
"5023","5017 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr, he said: Narrated to us Abu Ghassan, he said: Narrated to us Zuhayr, he said: Narrated to us Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed his sandals while praying, so those behind him removed their sandals. He said: ""What carried you to remove your sandals?"" They said: We saw you remove yours, so we removed ours. He said: ""Jibril informed me that in one of them was filth, so I removed them for that,"" and said: ""Do not remove your sandals."" This hadith was not narrated from Abu Hamzah except by Zuhayr."
"5024","5018 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn ar-Rabi' al-Burani, he said: Narrated to us Abu Ishaq al-Khumaysi Khazim ibn al-Husayn, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and behind Abu Bakr, and behind Umar, and behind Uthman, and behind Ali, and they would open the recitation with ""All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds,"" and would recite it ""Master of the Day of Judgment."" This hadith was not narrated from Malik ibn Dinar except by Abu Ishaq al-Khumaysi."
"5025","5019 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani, he said: Narrated to us Zuhayr, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: Abu Shu'ayb had a butcher slave; when he saw the hardship upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he ordered his slave to make for him food sufficing five, and sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to come as fifth of five. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and a man followed them; when he reached his door he said: ""You sent to me to come to you as fifth of five, and this one has followed us; if you permit him he will enter, otherwise he will return."" He said: I have permitted him, so he shall not return. This hadith was not narrated from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, except by Zuhayr. And ath-Thawri narrated it from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Mas'ud."
"5026","5020 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn ar-Rabi' al-Burani, he said: Narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Layth, from Ata, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The cupper and the cupped have broken fast."" This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Ahwas except by al-Hasan ibn ar-Rabi'."
"5027","5021 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us al-Hasan ibn ar-Rabi', he said: Narrated to us Dawud ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Attar, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The cupper and the cupped have broken fast."" This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Dawud al-Attar."
"5028","5022 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr, he said: Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Yunus, he said: Narrated to us Abu al-Ahwas, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, he said: Abu al-Yasar had a debt upon a man, and he came to him demanding it among his household. He said to the slave girl: Say he is not here. He heard his voice, and said: Come out, for I have heard your voice; so he came out to him. He said: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Hardship. He said: By Allah? He said: By Allah. He said: Go, and yours is upon you (i.e. it is remitted); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever grants respite to one in hardship, or remits for him, will be in the shade of Allah on the Day of Resurrection, or in the shelter of Allah."" This hadith was not narrated from Asim al-Ahwal except by Abu al-Ahwas."
"5029","5023 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, he said: Narrated to us al-Mas'udi, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, are there horses in Paradise? For I love horses. He said: ""If Allah admits you to Paradise, you will not wish to ride upon a red ruby that flies with you in Paradise wherever you wish."" Then another man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, are there camels in Paradise? He did not say to him what he said to his companion; he said: ""If Allah admits you to Paradise, you will have therein whatever your soul desires and your eye delights in."" This hadith was not narrated from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, except by al-Mas'udi."
"5030","5024 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Asim ibn Ali, he said: Narrated to us al-Mas'udi, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have a Hawd (fountain), from such to such, in it vessels numbering the stars, whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, cooler than snow, more fragrant than musk; whoever drinks from it will never thirst, and whoever does not drink from it will never be quenched."" This hadith was not narrated from Adi ibn Thabit except by al-Mas'udi."
"5031","5025 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Yazid ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Ma'ni, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bishr, he said: I heard Junayd ibn al-Ala ibn Abi Hurayrah mention, from Muhammad ibn Sa'id, from Ismail ibn Ubaydullah, from Umm ad-Darda, from Abu ad-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Free yourselves from the concerns of this world as much as you can, for whoever's greatest concern is this world, Allah scatters his estate and places his poverty before his eyes; and whoever's greatest concern is the Hereafter, Allah gathers his affairs for him, places his richness in his heart, and no servant turns with his heart to Allah except that Allah makes the hearts of the believers come to him with love and mercy, and Allah is swifter to him with every good."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu ad-Darda except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Bishr alone transmitted it."
"5032","5026 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Khalid ibn Khidash, he said: Narrated to us Sadaqah ibn Abi Sahl Abu Sahl al-Huna'i, he said: Narrated to me Kathir Abu al-Fadl, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: I came to Abu ad-Darda while he was in Syria, and he said: What brought you, O my son, to this land, and what concerned you with it? I said: Nothing brought me but maintaining what was between you and my father. He took my hand and seated me, and I leaned against him. Then he said: Evil is the hour of lying upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""No Muslim commits a sin, then performs ablution, then prays two rak'ahs, or four, obligatory or otherwise, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that Allah forgives him."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu ad-Darda except with this chain; Sadaqah ibn Abi Sahl alone transmitted it."
"5033","5027 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Khalid ibn Khidash, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Wahb, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani, from his father, from Abu Abd ar-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."" This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except with this chain; Abdullah ibn Ayyash alone transmitted it."
"5034","5028 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Khalid ibn Khidash, he said: Narrated to us Abd ar-Razzaq, he said: Narrated to me Bishr ibn Rafi' al-Harithi, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no might nor power except with Allah; a remedy for ninety-nine ailments, the least of them worry."" This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except by Bishr ibn Rafi'; Abd ar-Razzaq alone transmitted it."
"5035","5029 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Qadi, he said: Narrated to us Hibban ibn Ali, from Sa'd ibn Tarif, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Khawlah bint Qays, wife of Hamzah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) owed a wasq of dates to a man of Banu Sa'idah, and he came demanding it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man of the Ansar to pay him, and he paid him dates inferior to his, and he refused to accept it, and said: Do you reject (the order of) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; and who is more entitled to justice than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) filled with tears, then he said: ""He spoke truth; who is more entitled to justice than me? Allah does not sanctify a nation in which its weak does not take his right from its strong without being made to stammer."" Then he said: ""O Khawlah, promise him, treat him kindly, and pay him; for there is no creditor who leaves his debtor satisfied except that the beasts of the earth and the fish of the seas send blessings upon him, and there is no servant who delays his creditor while able, except that Allah writes upon him each day and night a sin."" This hadith is not narrated from Khawlah except with this chain; Hibban ibn Ali alone transmitted it."
"5036","5030 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Waddah ibn Yahya an-Nahshali, he said: Narrated to us Abu Mu'awiyah, from Umar ibn Bashir, from Imran ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Alqamah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order Bilal to chant slowly in the adhan and hasten in the iqamah. This hadith was not narrated from Umar ibn Bashir except by Abu Mu'awiyah, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"5037","5031 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Shihab ibn Abbad al-Abdi, he said: Narrated to us Dawud ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Attar, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling animal for animal on credit. This hadith was not connected from Ma'mar except by Dawud al-Attar and Sufyan ath-Thawri; Shihab alone transmitted the hadith of Dawud, and Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah alone transmitted the hadith of Sufyan ath-Thawri, from Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri."
"5038","5032 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Jurayj and Ismail ibn Muslim, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked in the year of Hajj about raml, and he said: ""Indeed Allah has prescribed sa'y upon you, so perform sa'y."""
"5039","5033 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from A'ishah, she said: As if I see the glisten of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he is in ihram."
"5040","5034 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What of clothes shall I wear when I intend ihram? He said: ""Do not wear the shirt, nor the qaba', nor the turban, nor the trousers, nor the khuffs, unless you have no sandals; if you have no sandals then wear the khuffs; and do not wear any garment touched by saffron or wars."""
"5041","5035 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Sufyan, from Ayyub as-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What shall the muhrim wear of clothes? He said: ""He shall not wear the shirt, nor the turban, nor the burnus, nor the trousers, nor the khuffs, unless he finds no sandals, then let him wear his khuffs and cut them below the ankles; and let him not wear a garment dyed with saffron or wars."""
"5042","5036 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from A'ishah, she said: I used to perfume the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before he entered ihram, and before he poured forth (from Mina) when he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"5043","5037 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram after Fajr when his mount stood upright with him."
"5044","5038 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said talbiyah he would say: ""Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; labbayk, no partner have You, labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You."""
"5045","5039 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I learned the talbiyah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; labbayk, no partner have You, labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You."""
"5046","5040 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: I learned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; labbayk, no partner have You, labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You."""
"5047","5041 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which Hajj is best? He said: ""The loud (ajj) and the flowing (thajj),"" i.e. raising the voice in talbiyah and shedding blood of sacrifice."
"5048","5042 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir, he said: When we ascended we would say takbir, and when we descended we would say tasbih."
"5049","5043 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Khusayf, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, regarding Allah's saying: ""Hajj is months well-known,"" he said: ""Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa'dah, and ten of Dhu al-Hijjah; Hajj is not undertaken except in them."""
"5050","5044 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Touching them wipes away sins,"" meaning the two corners."
"5051","5045 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, he began with the Black Stone and touched it, then ran three circuits and walked four circuits, then recited: ""And take the station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer,"" then came to the Maqam and prayed two rak'ahs beside it."
"5052","5046 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abis ibn Rabi'ah, from Umar, that he said to the Stone: ""By Allah, I know you are a stone, and were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would not kiss you."" Then he kissed it."
"5053","5047 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A'la, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, he said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab kissing the Black Stone and saying: I saw Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tender toward you."
"5054","5048 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever wishes may run (raml), and whoever wishes may not run; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only ordered raml to show the mushriks their strength."
"5055","5049 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, and the mushriks [...], the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to run to show them that they had strength. When they passed the Yemeni corner he said: ""Hasten""; so they walked until they reached the Black Stone."
"5056","5050 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu at-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas, he said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""The people have spoken that you have perished of hunger and emaciation; so when you enter, run three circuits so the people see that you have strength."" So we did."
"5057","5051 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Kathir ibn Jumhan, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar while he was walking in the valley, and said: O Ibn Umar, you order us to hasten (sa'y) while you walk? He said: If I walked, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walk; and if I hastened, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hasten; and I am an old man."
"5058","5052 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: I said to A'ishah: I see no sin upon me if I do not circumambulate between as-Safa and al-Marwah. She said: Why? I said: Because I heard Him say: ""Whoever performs Hajj of the House or Umrah, there is no sin upon him to circumambulate them."" She said: It is not so; had it been as you say, it would have been: no sin upon him not to circumambulate them. The Hajj of one who does not circumambulate between as-Safa and al-Marwah is not righteous. This verse was only revealed because when they entered ihram in Jahiliyyah for Manat, it was not lawful for them to circumambulate between as-Safa and al-Marwah; so Allah revealed: ""Indeed as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah; whoever performs Hajj of the House or Umrah, there is no sin upon him to circumambulate them."" So circumambulating them is among the rites of Allah."
"5059","5053 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ya'la ibn Umayyah, that he circumambulated with Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Umar would touch the Black Stone, and Ya'la would touch all the corners. Umar said: ""Did you perform Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"" He said: Yes. He said: ""And did you see him touching all the corners?"" He said: No."
"5060","5054 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr, he said: Narrated to us Mu'awiyah ibn Amr, he said: Narrated to us al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ya'la ibn Umayyah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a cloak scented with yellow perfume, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for Umrah, what shall I do? He said: He lowered his head from him long until we thought revelation had come to him, then said: ""Where is the questioner about Umrah? Remove your cloak, wash off the yellow, and do in Umrah as you do in Hajj."" These hadiths were not narrated from al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah except by Mu'awiyah ibn Amr."
"5061","5055 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti, he said: Narrated to us Hushaym, he said: Narrated to us Mansur ibn Zadhan, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Modesty is part of faith, and faith is in Paradise; and obscenity is part of harshness, and harshness is in the Fire."" This hadith was not narrated from Hushaym, from Mansur, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, except by Sa'id ibn Sulayman; and others narrated it from Mansur, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn."
"5062","5056 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bind knowledge? He said: ""Yes."" I said: And what is its binding? He said: ""Writing."" This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal."
"5063","5057 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave,"" they said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave,"" they said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? After three he said: ""And those who shorten."" This hadith was not narrated from Ata except by Abdullah ibn al-Mu'ammal."
"5064","5058 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Abd as-Samad ibn Sulayman al-Azraq, he said: Narrated to us al-Khasib ibn Jahdar, from Habib ibn Hayyan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that an effeminate man with dyed hands and feet was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began striking him with their sandals. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware this one and his companions for your women."" They said: Shall we not kill him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""No; I have been forbidden from killing those who pray."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri except with this chain; al-Khasib ibn Jahdar alone transmitted it."
"5065","5059 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Sulayman, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, he said: Narrated to us Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever builds for Allah a house in which Allah is worshipped, from lawful wealth, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise of pearl and ruby."" This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except by Sulayman ibn Dawud; Sa'id ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"5066","5060 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Walid, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""In Paradise is a gate called ad-Duha; when the Day of Resurrection comes, a caller will call: Where are those who used to persist in Duha prayer? This is your gate, so enter it by the mercy of Allah."""
"5067","5061 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Walid, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""By the One who sent me with the truth, this world will not end until there befall them collapse, transformation, and pelting."" They said: When is that, O Prophet of Allah? He said: ""When you see women riding saddles, singing girls multiply, false testimony is borne, those who pray drink in vessels of the people of shirk, gold and silver, men suffice themselves with men and women with women; then seek protection and prepare."" And he gestured with his hand, placing it on his forehead, shielding his face."
"5068","5062 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Walid, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Leave the beards full, take from the mustaches, pluck the armpits, and beware the two clefts (i.e. private openings regarding impurity)."""
"5069","5063 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Walid, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abu Bakr: ""How do you pray witr?"" He said: I pray witr at the beginning of the night. He said: ""Prudent, cautious."" Then he asked Umar: ""O Abu Hafs, how do you pray witr?"" He said: I pray witr at the end of the night. He said: ""Strong, aided."""
"5070","5064 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Walid, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three traits, whoever has them, Allah will reckon him an easy reckoning and admit him to Paradise by His mercy."" They said: What are they, O Prophet of Allah, may our fathers and mothers be ransomed for you? He said: ""You give to whoever deprived you, join whoever cut you, and pardon whoever wronged you."" He said: If I do this, what is for me, O Prophet of Allah? He said: ""Allah will admit you to Paradise."""
"5071","5065 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Bishr ibn al-Walid, he said: Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, whom shall I honor? He said: ""Your mother."" She said: Then whom? He said: ""Then your mother."" She said: Then whom? He said: ""Then your mother."" She said: Then whom? He said: ""Then your father."" These hadiths were not narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except by Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami."
"5072","5066 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Yazid ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Ma'ni, he said: Narrated to us Abd ar-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, from his father, he said: A guest alighted upon Jabir ibn Abdullah, and he brought them bread and vinegar, and said: Eat, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""What an excellent condiment is vinegar; destruction to the people that they belittle what is presented to them, and destruction to the man that he belittles what is in his house to present to his companions."" This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman except by al-Muharibi."
"5073","5067 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Faraj al-Baghdadi, he said: Narrated to us Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn az-Zibriqan, he said: Narrated to us Musa ibn Ubaydah, he said: Narrated to me Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, he said: Narrated to me Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows."" And he said: ""Between the lone one and the congregation are twenty-five degrees."" This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Zayd except with this chain; Muhammad ibn az-Zibriqan alone transmitted it."
"5074","5068 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani, he said: Narrated to us Sharik, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: By what do I know that you are the Messenger of Allah? He said: ""What if I call this cluster from this palm, will you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" He said: Yes. So he called the cluster, and it began descending from the palm until it fell to the ground, then hopping until it came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to it: ""Return,"" so it returned, then went back to its place. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. This hadith was not narrated from Simak except by Sharik."
"5075","5069 - Narrated to us Muhammad ibn an-Nadr al-Azdi, he said: Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani, he said: Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Umm Nasr al-Muharibiyyah, she said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the jallalah (animal feeding on filth), and he said: ""Does it not graze pasture and eat trees?"" Perhaps he said: Yes. He said: ""Then eat of its meat."" This hadith is not narrated from Umm Nasr al-Muharibiyyah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar alone transmitted it."
"5076","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Ma'ni narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, who said: Anas said: When we were forbidden from initiating questions to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it used to please us that an intelligent Bedouin man would come and ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were with him. While we were like that, a Bedouin came and said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and claimed that you claim that Allah sent you. He said: ""He spoke the truth."" He said: By the One Who set up the mountains, raised the sky, and spread out the earth, did Allah send you? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."" He said: Your messenger claims that you claim that five prayers in the day and night are upon us? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He spoke the truth."" He said: By the One Who sent you, did Allah command you with this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."" He said: Your messenger claims that you claim that fasting a month in the year is upon us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He spoke the truth."" He said: By the One Who sent you, did Allah command you with this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."" He said: Your messenger claimed that you claim that zakat in our wealth is upon us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He spoke the truth."" He said: By the One Who sent you, did Allah command you with this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."" He said: Your messenger claims that you claim that Hajj to the House is upon us for whoever is able to find a way to it. He said: ""He spoke the truth."" He said: By the One Who sent you, did Allah command you with this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."" He said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I will not leave anything of them nor go beyond them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the Bedouin is truthful, he will enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit al-Bunani except Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah."
"5077","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what Allah has obligated upon me of prayer? He said: Allah has obligated upon His servants five prayers. He said: Is there anything before them or after them? He said: Allah has obligated upon His servants five prayers. He said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, I will not add anything to them nor decrease anything from them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will enter Paradise if he is truthful. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Khalid ibn Qays; Nuh ibn Qays is alone in narrating it."
"5078","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The expiation of sins is remorse."
"5079","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin and then He would forgive them. These two hadiths are not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri is alone in narrating them."
"5080","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the people of the dhimmah: They keep whatever land, slaves, and livestock they accepted Islam with, and nothing is upon them concerning any of that except sadaqah. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Layth ibn Abi Sulaym; Musa ibn A'yan is alone in narrating it."
"5081","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, that he heard Anas ibn Malik reporting from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the prayer is established and one of you is fasting, let him begin with dinner before the Maghrib prayer, and do not rush away from your dinner. No one said in this hadith, 'and one of you is fasting, let him begin with dinner before the Maghrib prayer,' except Amr ibn al-Harith; Musa ibn A'yan is alone in narrating it."
"5082","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Zaidah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sulaym ibn Khaldah al-Ansari, from Abu Qatadah, who said: I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among the people. So I sat down, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What prevented you from bowing two rak'ahs before sitting? He said: I saw you sitting and the people sitting. He said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rak'ahs. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Yahya except Zaidah."
"5083","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Zaidah narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, saying: Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The sitting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the two rak'ahs was as if upon heated stones."
"5084","Muhammad ibn al-Nadir al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Zaidah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, who said: I heard Adi ibn Thabit saying: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Isha with 'By the fig and the olive.' Zaidah did not narrate with a chain from Mis'ar except these two hadiths."
"5085","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib, the freed slave of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, saying: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went to his bed every night, would join his palms, then blow into them, and recite into them: 'Say: He is Allah, the One,' and 'Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak,' and 'Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind,' then wipe with them whatever he could of his body, beginning with them over his head and face and what faces him of his body, doing that three times. No one narrated this hadith in its completeness from al-Zuhri except Uqayl ibn Khalid; al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah is alone in narrating it."
"5086","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dulabi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a military expedition, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take many sandals, for a man remains as if riding as long as he wears sandals. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"5087","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bashir al-Kindi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Kathir al-Nawwa, who said: Abu Maryam al-Ansari narrated to me, and he was one hundred and fifty years old, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: Your bringing joy to a believer, satisfying his hunger, clothing his nakedness, or fulfilling a need for him. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir al-Nawwa except Ali ibn Hashim; Muhammad ibn Bashir is alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Umar except with this chain."
"5088","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, saying: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, saying: My father Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to me - and I used to call my grandfather my father - saying: Jabir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, saying: The family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a servant who served them, called Barrah. A man met her and said to her: O Barrah, cover your little hairs, for Muhammad will not avail you anything against Allah. She informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came out dragging his cloak with his cheeks reddened - and we, the Ansar, recognized his anger by the dragging of his cloak and the redness of his cheeks - so we took up arms, then came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, command us as you wish; by the One Who sent you with the truth, if you commanded us regarding our mothers, fathers, and children, we would carry out your word concerning them. So he ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: Who am I? We said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes, but who am I? We said: You are Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf. He said: I am the master of the children of Adam, and no boast; the first for whom the earth will split open, and no boast; the first from whose head the dust will be shaken off, and no boast; the first to enter Paradise, and no boast. What is the matter with people who claim that my kinship does not benefit? It is not as they claimed; I will intercede, and my intercession will be accepted, until even those for whom I intercede will intercede and their intercession will be accepted, until even Iblis will stretch forth hope in intercession. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, except al-Qasim ibn Abdullah; Ubayd ibn Ishaq is alone in narrating it."
"5089","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A caller calls out every morning: O Allah, give one who spends a replacement, and give one who withholds ruin. No one narrated this hadith except Ubayd ibn Ishaq."
"5090","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood. No one narrated this hadith from Kamil except Ubayd ibn Ishaq."
"5091","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih and Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people with Allah is the one with two faces, who comes to these with one face and to these with another face. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, except Qays; Ubayd ibn Ishaq is alone in narrating it."
"5092","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Abu Maryam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, by what will you recognize your ummah? He said: Radiant with white marks from the traces of purification. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Maryam and Ibn Fudayl, and no one narrated it from Ibn Fudayl except al-Sari ibn Asim."
"5093","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Utbah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you, for there is no servant who sleeps in a state of purity except that an angel spends the night with him in his bedding; he does not turn at any hour of the night except that he says: O Allah, forgive Your servant, for he slept in purity. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Abi Rabah except al-Abbas ibn Utbah; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in narrating it."
"5094","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch intimately while fasting, and kiss while fasting, and which of you is like him? He was the most in control of his desire among you. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Muhammad ibn Talhah and Muhammad ibn Aban."
"5095","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a caravan that had arrived, and profited therein ounces of gold, and gave it in charity to the widows of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, and said: I will not buy anything for which I do not have its price. No one rendered this hadith well from Sharik except Sa'id ibn Sulayman and Amr ibn Awn."
"5096","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: That the belly of one of you be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu Ja'far al-Razi."
"5097","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Asim, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah hates the eloquent among men who curls his tongue as cattle curl with it. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except with this chain; Nafi ibn Umar is alone in narrating it."
"5098","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim al-Madani narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Charity does not decrease wealth, and Allah does not increase a man through pardon except in honor, and no one humbles himself except that Allah raises him. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim except Affan."
"5099","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from Zubayd, from al-Sha'bi, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while I was the seventh of seven from Quraysh, and said: Do you not hear? Three times: There will be rulers or leaders over you, so whoever enters upon them and believes their lies and aids them in their wrongdoing is not of me and I am not of him, and I am free of him; and whoever does not enter upon them, nor believe their lies, nor aid them in their wrongdoing, is of me and I am of him, and he will meet me and be with me. No one narrated this hadith from Zubayd except Muhammad ibn Talhah."
"5100","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who is moderate in spending will not become poor. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim al-Hajari except Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"5101","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among trees there is a tree that is like the Muslim man; it is the date palm. No one narrated this hadith from Zubayd except Muhammad ibn Talhah."
"5102","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: 'I swear by this city' - he said: Makkah; 'and you are free in this city' - he said: Makkah; 'and by the father and what he begot' - he said: Adam; 'We have certainly created man in hardship' - he said: In uprightness, in erect posture. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit Abu al-Miqdam except his son Amr ibn Thabit."
"5103","Muhammad ibn Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abdullah ibn Abi Utbah, from Aishah, that charity meat was given to Barirah, and she gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said to him: It is from charity meat. He said: It is charity for her, and a gift for us. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Utbah except Humayd; Hammad ibn Salamah is alone in narrating it."
"5104","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: The family of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate their fill of wheat bread until he passed away, and no leftover crumb was ever lifted from the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he passed away. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except Muhammad ibn Talhah."
"5105","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Umar narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command marriage and strongly forbid celibacy, and would say: Marry the loving and fertile, for I will boast of your numbers before the prophets on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Hafs, the nephew of Anas, except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"5106","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, saying: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Mijlaz, who said: Ibn Umar said: As for us, we used to give the charity of Fitr as dates. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Abthar."
"5107","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us, saying: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever speaks about the Quran by his opinion and is right has erred. Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm did not narrate with a chain from Abu Imran al-Jawni except this hadith."
"5108","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Sa'd ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Nuh ibn Abi Bilal, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: 'All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds' is seven verses, one of them being 'In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate,' and it is the seven oft-repeated, and the Magnificent Quran, and it is the Mother of the Quran and the Opening of the Book. No one narrated this hadith from Nuh ibn Abi Bilal except Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far; Ali ibn Thabit is alone in narrating it."
"5109","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Adhin, from Makhul, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant does not believe with complete faith until he leaves lying in jest and disputation even if he is truthful. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Mansur ibn Adhin; Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah is alone in narrating it."
"5110","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Qatari al-Khashshab narrated to us, from Abd al-Warith, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's food is placed before him, and it is not lifted until he is forgiven. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, for what is that? He said: He says 'In the name of Allah' when it is placed, and 'Praise be to Allah' when it is lifted."
"5111","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Qatari al-Khashshab narrated to us, from Abd al-Warith, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the end of time, my ummah will become three groups: a group that worships Allah sincerely, a group that worships Allah for show, and a group that worships Allah to consume people thereby. When Allah gathers them on the Day of Resurrection, He will say to the one who consumed people: By My might and majesty, what did you intend by My worship? He will say: By Your might and majesty, to consume people thereby. He will say: Nothing you gathered benefited you at all; take him to the Fire. Then He will say to the one who worshipped Him for show: By My might and majesty, what did you intend by My worship? He will say: By Your might and majesty, showing off to people. He will say: Nothing of it ascended to Me; take him to the Fire. Then He will say to the one who worshipped Him sincerely: By My might and majesty, what did you intend by My worship? He will say: By Your might and majesty, You know better than I; I intended thereby Your remembrance and Your Face. He will say: My servant has spoken the truth; take him to Paradise. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abd al-Warith except Qatari al-Khashshab; Ubayd ibn Ishaq al-Attar is alone in narrating them."
"5112","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nafi, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, from Aishah and Hafsah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days except over a husband. No one narrated this hadith from Fulayh except Surayj ibn al-Nu'man."
"5113","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered in three ways: desiring, fearing, two on a camel, three on a camel, ten on a camel, and the Fire will gather the rest of them; it rests with them where they rest at noon, stays with them where they stay at night, rises with them where they rise in the morning, and evenings with them where they evening. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Tawus except Wuhayb and Ibn Jurayj; al-Hajjaj al-A'war is alone in narrating it from Ibn Jurayj."
"5114","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah raises the servant to a rank, and he says: O Lord, how is this rank for me? He says: By your child's seeking forgiveness for you. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"5115","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Call upon Allah while you are certain of the answer, and know that Allah does not answer a supplication from a heedless, inattentive heart. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Salih al-Murri."
"5116","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Kulthum ibn Jabr, from Khuthaym ibn Marwan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: the mosque of al-Khayf, the Sacred Mosque, and this mosque of mine. No one narrated this hadith from Kulthum ibn Jabr except Hammad ibn Salamah, and 'the mosque of al-Khayf' is not mentioned regarding tying saddles except in this hadith."
"5117","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih and from Humayd al-A'raj, from Mujahid, from Aishah, that she used to rub semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he would pray in it. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Ibn Abi Najih and Humayd al-A'raj, and no one narrated it from them except Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd."
"5118","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, that he heard Ata narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be lenient and you will be treated leniently. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"5119","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate his fill of wheat bread twice in a day until he met Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except Hammad ibn Zayd."
"5120","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Mujalid narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are today upon a religion, and I will boast of your numbers before the nations, so do not walk backward after me. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except Hammad ibn Zayd."
"5121","Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The charities of the desert people are taken at their waters and courtyards. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr except Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr; Abdullah ibn Salih is alone in narrating it."
"5122","Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: A lizard was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not eat it. Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not feed it to the poor? He said: Do not feed them what you do not eat. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except Hammad ibn Salamah and Sufyan al-Thawri."
"5123","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Hilal al-Wazzan, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hassan: Lampoon the polytheists; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit. No one narrated this hadith from Hilal al-Wazzan except Ismail ibn Mujalid; Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan is alone in narrating it, and Ali ibn al-Madini narrated it from Sabalan."
"5124","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: al-Husayn ibn Ubaydullah al-Ijli narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to relieve himself, would not lift his garment until he drew near the ground. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; al-Husayn ibn Ubaydullah al-Ijli is alone in narrating it."
"5125","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Salam ibn Salih al-Harawi narrated to us, saying: Abbad al-Awwam narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Zayd, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love your beloved moderately, perhaps he will become hateful to you someday, and hate whom you hate moderately, perhaps he will become beloved to you someday. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Umar except with this chain; Abbad ibn al-Awwam is alone in narrating it."
"5126","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Fihri narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love your beloved moderately, perhaps he will become hateful to you someday, and hate whom you hate moderately, perhaps he will become beloved to you someday. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Fihri is alone in narrating it."
"5127","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows so your hearts become straight, and press together so you show mercy to one another. Surayj said: Press together means crowd together in prayer; others said: press together means maintain ties. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Mujalid, nor from Mujalid except Abu Khalid al-Ahmar; Surayj ibn Yunus is alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"5128","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Dajjal was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: His mother will give birth to him while she is cast aside in her grave, and when she gives birth to him, women will bear the sinful. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Tawus except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi."
"5129","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: The practice of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran with the dowries of women as twelve ounces, the ounce being forty dirhams, and that is four hundred and eighty; and the practice of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran in the bath of janabah as a sa', the sa' being eight ratls; and ablution with a mudd, the mudd being two ratls; and his practice ran in the tenth that there is no zakat in less than five wasqs, the wasq being sixty sa's with this sa', and that is three hundred sa's. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Salih ibn Musa."
"5130","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Aishah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Madinah al-Darimi - and he had companionship - who said: Two men from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when they met, would not part until one of them recited to the other: 'By time, indeed mankind is in loss,' then one of them would greet the other. Ali ibn al-Madini said: The name of Abu Madinah is Abdullah ibn Hisn. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Madinah except with this chain; Hammad ibn Salamah is alone in narrating it."
"5131","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Qadi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Qays, from Ishaq ibn Abi al-Kahtalah - Muhammad ibn Talhah said: I think it is from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not see Jibril in his form except twice: once he asked him to show himself in his form, so he showed him and filled the horizon; and the second when he was with him as he ascended, in His saying: 'Then he approached and descended, and was at a distance of two bow lengths or nearer, and revealed to His servant what He revealed.' When Jibril sensed his Lord, blessed and exalted, he returned to his form, and that is His saying: 'And he certainly saw him in another descent, at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, near it is the Garden of Refuge,' up to His saying: 'He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord.' He said: The creation of Jibril, peace be upon him. This hadith is not narrated from Ishaq ibn Abi al-Kahtalah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif is alone in narrating it."
"5132","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: We were once with Abu Usamah, and the mustamli said: Turn to me. Al-Ahwas ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Rashid ibn Sa'd and Abu al-Zahiriyyah, who said: We heard Abu al-Darda saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us while we were digging a grave, and said: What are you doing? We said: We are digging a grave for this black man. He said: His death brought him to his soil. Abu Usamah said: Do you know, O people of Kufa, why I narrated this hadith to you? Because Abu Bakr and Umar were created from the soil of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain; Abu Usamah is alone in narrating it."
"5133","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Hammad ibn Furafisah al-Balkhi narrated to us, saying: Attab ibn Muhammad ibn Shawdhab, the nephew of Abdullah ibn Shawdhab, narrated to us, from Isa al-Azraq, from Matar al-Warraq, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he put his hand under his chin and ran his fingers through, and I said: What is this? He said: Thus my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me. No one narrated this hadith from Matar al-Warraq except Isa al-Azraq, nor from Isa except Attab ibn Muhammad; Dawud ibn Hammad is alone in narrating it."
"5134","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Hassan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: I sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and wept. He said: What makes you weep? If you desire to join me, let the provision of a rider of this world suffice you, and do not mix with the rich. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Salih ibn Hassan; Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah is alone in narrating it."
"5135","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Bazi' Abu al-Khalil narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is told of a virtue from Allah and does not believe in it will not attain it. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Bazi' Abu al-Khalil."
"5136","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zadahan, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the Quran, memorizes it by heart and preserves it, Allah will admit him to Paradise and grant his intercession for a number of his household, all of whom deserved the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Hafs ibn Sulayman is alone in narrating it."
"5137","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abdullah ibn Yahya al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Harun ibn Antarah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will continue to pray these four rak'ahs before Asr until it walks upon the earth forgiven, a certain forgiveness. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"5138","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets a prayer and remembers it while he is with the imam, let him complete his prayer, make up what he forgot, then repeat the one he prayed with the imam. No one raised this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman; al-Tarjuman is alone in narrating it."
"5139","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, saying: Hakim ibn Nafi al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two prostrations of forgetfulness suffice for everything: addition and decrease. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Hakim ibn Nafi."
"5140","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, saying: Layth ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ghayl, then said: Did it harm Persia and Rome? That is when a man comes to his wife while she is nursing. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Abi Salamah except Abu Awanah; Layth ibn Hammad is alone in narrating it."
"5141","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abu Awn, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, who said: I heard Muawiyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every sin, Allah may forgive it, except a man who dies a disbeliever, or a man who kills a believer deliberately. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr ibn Yazid except al-Mu'afa ibn Imran; al-Hasan ibn Bishr is alone in narrating it."
"5142","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Bilal al-Tamimi narrated to us, saying: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child is of the father's earning."
"5143","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Shuja' ibn Makhlad narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah al-Saffar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to join Sha'ban with Ramadan. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Yusuf ibn Atiyyah; Shuja' is alone in narrating it."
"5144","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not blow into food nor drink. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Hafs ibn Sulayman."
"5145","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Jubayr ibn Hayyah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped aside and I stepped aside with him. I drew near him and he said: Do you have water? I said: Yes. So he washed his hands and face, and went to wash his hands while wearing a cloak that was tight, so he brought his hand out from under the cloak and washed it, then wiped over his leather socks, then came to pray while Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was leading the people in prayer. When they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they cleared their throats, and he went to step back, but he signaled to him: Go on. This hadith is not narrated from Jubayr ibn Hayyah except with this chain; Amr ibn al-Zubayr is alone in narrating it."
"5146","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id, from Abdullah ibn Ka'b al-Himyari, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May one who is fasting kiss? He said: Ask this one - to Umm Salamah, who was sitting. She said: He does so. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? He said: By Allah, I am indeed the most fearful of Allah among you and the most pious. This hadith is not narrated from Umar ibn Abi Salamah except with this chain; Amr ibn al-Harith is alone in narrating it."
"5147","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, saying: al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Arafah supplicating, raising his hands, when the camel's halter fell from his hand, so he took it, then raised his hands supplicating. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is earnest beseeching and humility. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except al-Fadl ibn Musa."
"5148","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, saying: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Sa'd ibn al-Mundhir, from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on the day of Uhud until, when he passed Thaniyyat al-Wada', he saw a compact battalion of two armies, and said: Who are these? They said: This is Abdullah ibn Ubayy with six hundred of his freedmen from the Jews of Banu Qaynuqa. He said: Have they accepted Islam? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Order them to return, for we do not seek the aid of polytheists against polytheists. No one rendered this hadith well from Muhammad ibn Amr except al-Fadl ibn Musa and Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi."
"5149","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell what you do not have. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Atiq except Hammad ibn Zayd; Khalid ibn Khidash is alone in narrating it."
"5150","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, saying: Abu Awn, the seller of waterskins, narrated to us, saying: Sadus, the seller of sabiri cloth, narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When creatures meet on the Day of Resurrection, and the people of Paradise are admitted to Paradise and the people of the Fire to the Fire, a caller will call on the Day of Resurrection: O people of the gathering, waive the wrongs among you, and your reward is upon Me. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Sadus; Abu Awn is alone in narrating it."
"5151","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Aswad, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Announce marriage. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except with this chain; Ibn Wahb is alone in narrating it."
"5152","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Simsar narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, saying: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Bassam al-Sayrafi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Suhayb al-Faqir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some people of my ummah will be punished for their sins and remain in the Fire as long as Allah wills them to remain, then the people of polytheism will taunt them, saying: We do not see that what you differed from us in, of your affirmation and faith, benefited you. Then no monotheist will remain except that Allah brings him out. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: 'Perhaps those who disbelieved will wish they had been Muslims.' No one narrated this hadith from Bassam al-Sayrafi except Hatim; Muhammad ibn Abbad is alone in narrating it."
"5153","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Mihran Abu Khalid al-Khabbaz narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: When the news of the death of the Negus came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray over him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, do you pray over an Abyssinian? So Allah revealed: 'And indeed, among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what was revealed to you.' No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman."
"5154","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, saying: al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, saying: Abu Zumayl narrated to me, from Malik ibn Marthad, from his father, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Neither the dusty earth bears nor the green sky shades one with a tongue more truthful than Abu Dharr, resembling Isa son of Maryam. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah ibn Ammar except al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi."
"5155","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, saying: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn Abi Muhammad, from Bijad ibn Musa ibn Sa'd, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be collared with it from seven earths; Allah accepts from him neither sarf nor adl; and whoever claims belonging to other than his father or other than his masters has disbelieved. No one narrated this hadith from Bijad ibn Musa except Hamzah ibn Abi Muhammad; Hatim ibn Ismail is alone in narrating it."
"5156","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd al-Bazzaz narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Hilal al-Bariqi narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, who said: I asked Usamah ibn Zayd: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travel when he poured forth from Arafat? He said: At a quick trot; when he found an opening, he galloped. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Asim ibn Hilal."
"5157","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Aishah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, all your wives have entered the House except me. He said: Go to your relatives, to Shaybah, and let him open the door for you. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib except Shu'ayb ibn Safwan."
"5158","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, saying: al-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Sallam, from Safinah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bravo, bravo, for five - how heavy they are in the Balance: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and a righteous child a man sends forth. This hadith is not narrated from Safinah except with this chain; al-Nadr ibn Muhammad is alone in narrating it."
"5159","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, saying: Abu Maryam narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ata, who said: Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dayli narrated to me, who said: Abdullah ibn Ijarah ibn Qays narrated to me, who said: I heard the Commander of the Believers, Ali ibn Abi Talib, while upon the minbar, saying: I drive away from the Hawd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two short hands of mine the disbelievers and hypocrites, as water-bearers drive strange camels from their troughs. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Ata except Abu Maryam; Muhammad ibn Qudamah is alone in narrating it, from Abu al-Jawwab."
"5160","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to me, saying: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd al-Ru'asi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Aishah, who said: I would tighten my waist-wrapper over me while menstruating, then enter with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) under his cover."
"5161","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Sufficient as a sin for a man is that he neglects those he supports."
"5162","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that debt comes before bequest, while you recite: 'After any bequest you make or debt.' And that full brothers from the same mother inherit to the exclusion of half-brothers from different mothers. No one narrated these hadiths from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd al-Ru'asi except his son Humayd; Yahya ibn Ayyub is alone in narrating them."
"5163","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, saying: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has three daughters, or the like of sisters, and shelters them and maintains them, Paradise becomes due for him. We said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. And we think had we said one, he would have said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Asim ibn Hilal."
"5164","Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, who said: al-Hasan used to come to Abu Hurayrah while a boy, kiss him, and say: By my father, the likeness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), broad between the shoulders."
"5165","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Salm ibn Qadim narrated to us, saying: Hashim ibn Isa al-Yazani narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on a servant who had a wrong against his brother concerning the soul or wealth, and came to him seeking his pardon before the Day of Resurrection, for there will be no dinar nor dirham there; there are only good deeds. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he has no good deeds? He said: Some of his sins will be taken and placed upon his sins. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Harith ibn Muslim, nor from al-Harith except Hashim ibn Isa; Salm ibn Qadim is alone in narrating it."
"5166","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us, saying: Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change white hair, but do not come near black, do not resemble your enemies among the polytheists, and the best of what you change white hair with is henna and katam. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Salm ibn Salim; Isa ibn Salim is alone in narrating it."
"5167","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abdullah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took gold in one hand and silk in the other and said: This is forbidden for the males of my ummah. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"5168","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Samti narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has servants whom He singles out with blessings for the benefit of other servants; He keeps them therein as long as they expend them, and when they withhold them, He strips them from them and transfers them to others. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Himsi."
"5169","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Amir ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Ammar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Layth, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that dogs are a nation among nations, I would command killing them; so kill of them every jet-black one. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Ammar ibn Muhammad; Amir ibn Sa'id is alone in narrating it."
"5170","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Hajib ibn al-Walid narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pass by boys, greet them, and supplicate for blessing for them."
"5171","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Muttalib al-Ijli narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah - raised - who said: The people of a house may have little food, yet their houses become illuminated. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, nor from al-Hasan except Abdullah ibn al-Muttalib; Abd al-Rahman is alone in narrating it."
"5172","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Hajib ibn al-Walid narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the sick person when he recovers and becomes healthy from his illness is like a hailstone falling from the sky in its purity. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Zuhri except al-Muwaqqari."
"5173","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Salm ibn Qadim narrated to us, saying: Hashim ibn Isa al-Yazani narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man leaves his house seeking knowledge except that Allah makes easy for him a path to Paradise. This hadith is not narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id except with this chain; Salm ibn Qadim is alone in narrating it."
"5174","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, saying: Hilal ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it pleases you to look at a bulky man obeyed among his people, look at this - meaning Uyaynah ibn Hisn. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah except Hilal ibn al-Jahm; Umar ibn Yunus is alone in narrating it."
"5175","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Waqid al-Saffar narrated to us, saying: I heard Isra'il narrating, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask Allah of His bounty, for Allah loves to be asked, and the best worship is awaiting relief. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Isra'il; Hammad ibn Waqid is alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Mas'ud except with this chain."
"5176","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn Ma'mar al-Qarqasani narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever acts for Allah in unity - if he is right, Allah accepts from him, and if he errs, He forgives him; and whoever acts for Allah in division - if he is right, Allah does not accept from him, and if he errs, he takes his seat in the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Zayd al-Ammi is alone in narrating it."
"5177","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Go forth in the morning as a scholar, a learner, a listener, or a lover, and do not be the fifth, lest you perish. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Ata ibn Muslim; Ubayd ibn Jannad is alone in narrating it."
"5178","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden of the gardens of Madinah and commanded me to close the door, so I closed it. A man came and knocked on the door, and he said: Open the door and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and that he will lead the ummah after me. So I opened the door, and it was Abu Bakr. Then I closed the door, and a man came and knocked on the door, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Anas, open the door and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and that he will lead the ummah after Abu Bakr. So I opened the door, and it was Umar, and I gave him glad tidings of Paradise and that he would lead the affair after Abu Bakr. Then I closed the door, and a man came and knocked on the door, and he said: O Anas, open the door and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and inform him that he will lead the ummah after Abu Bakr and Umar, and that a trial will befall him. And it was Uthman, so he praised Allah and said 'to Allah we belong and to Him we return,' then entered. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful except Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Musawir, Bakr ibn al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, and Utbah Abu Amr al-Muktib."
"5179","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Aishah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed upon a mat voluntarily, out of gratitude."
"5180","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aishah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has fever, let him pour cold water over himself before dawn for three nights. No one narrated these two hadiths from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, except Ibn Aishah, and the companions of Hammad narrated them from Hammad, from Humayd, from al-Hasan."
"5181","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two horned rams, eating in blackness, looking in blackness, and walking in blackness. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Sa'id with this wording except Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn; Hafs ibn Ghiyath is alone in narrating it."
"5182","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr Abu Ja'far al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Ubadah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you pray in his mosque, and not follow after mosques. No one narrated this hadith from Zuhayr except Ubadah ibn Ziyad."
"5183","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami al-Misri narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from Irak ibn Malik, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from al-Jarrah, the freedman of Umm Habibah, from Umm Habibah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell. No one narrated this hadith from Irak ibn Malik except Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah."
"5184","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from his father, from Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he missed anything of Ramadan, would make it up in the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sini is alone in narrating it."
"5185","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salim al-Qazzaz narrated to us, saying: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Harith al-Ukli, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: May Allah brighten a man who heard my saying and memorized it, for many a bearer of understanding is not understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys to one more understanding than him. Three things over which the heart of a Muslim man harbors no malice: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere advice to the rulers, and adhering to the congregation of the Muslims, for their supplication encompasses those behind them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith al-Ukli except al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, nor from al-Qasim except Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad; Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salim is alone in narrating it."
"5186","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran ibn Miqlas al-Misri narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Qatadah ibn Di'amah narrated to him, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised her that she would pray in the House, and commanded her to pray in the Hijr. She said: You promised me that I would pray in the House. He said: It is of the House; were it not that your people are recent in their break with polytheism, I would have joined it to the House. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Amr ibn al-Harith."
"5187","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran ibn Miqlas narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every letter mentioned of qunut in the Quran is obedience. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain."
"5188","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Amr al-Ash'athi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I circumambulated the House before stoning? He said: No harm. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman."
"5189","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Musa ibn Isa al-Sha'bi, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, saying: My uncle Zakariyya ibn Isa narrated to me, from the nephew of Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab, who said: Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel hastened him, combine these two prayers: Maghrib and Isha."
"5190","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Azhari narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Musa ibn Isa al-Sha'bi narrated to us, saying: My uncle Zakariyya ibn Isa narrated to me, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when returning from Makkah, would say takbir three times, saying: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable; returning, repenting, worshipping, prostrating, to our Lord praising; Allah has fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone."
"5191","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Azhari narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Musa ibn Isa narrated to us, from his uncle Zakariyya ibn Isa, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar found severe cold while traveling, so he commanded a caller to announce: Pray in your dwellings, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when it was like this, command that."
"5192","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Azhari narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Musa ibn Isa narrated to us, from his uncle Zakariyya ibn Isa, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar, when he arrived from a journey, would halt at al-Batha at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to halt there."
"5193","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Azhari narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Musa ibn Isa narrated to us, from his uncle Zakariyya ibn Isa, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the call for the dawn prayer was made, would bow two light rak'ahs before the prayer was established. These hadiths are not narrated from al-Zuhri except with this chain; Zakariyya ibn Isa al-Sha'bi is alone in narrating them."
"5194","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Sufyan al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, saying: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of the family of Talhah, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I lay across in front of him, and I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from a single vessel. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of the family of Talhah, except Isra'il, nor from Isra'il except Abu Ahmad; al-Qawariri is alone in narrating it."
"5195","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Sufyan al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Salim, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and when we drew near Madinah I wanted to hasten, and he said: Wait until the woman whose husband is absent shaves her pubic hair and the disheveled one combs her hair. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Salim except Hushaym; al-Qawariri is alone in narrating it."
"5196","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj Abu Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Shurayh ibn Hani, who said: I asked Aishah about wiping over the leather socks. She said: Go to Ali, for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I went to Ali, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and night for the resident. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid except Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad; Abdullah ibn Umar is alone in narrating it."
"5197","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad al-Hamdani narrated to us, saying: Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Musli, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of fine appearance and pleasant scent came to him and greeted. He said: O Prophet of Allah, may I draw near you? He said: Draw near. So he drew near until he almost touched him, then said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me what Islam is? He said: That you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, give zakat, and fast Ramadan. He said: If I do this, am I a Muslim? He said: Yes. The man said: You spoke the truth. He said: O Prophet of Allah, inform me what faith is? He said: That you believe in Allah, His angels, His Book, His messengers, the Resurrection, and believe in all of the decree, its good and its evil. He said: If I do that, am I a believer? He said: Yes. The man said: You spoke the truth. He said: What is excellence? He said: That you fear Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you, and you love for people what you love for yourself. He said: If I do that, am I excellent? He said: Yes. The man said: You spoke the truth. The man said: When is the Hour? He said: The one asked knows no more of it than the questioner, except that it has signs and marks. He said: What are they? He said: When you see the barefoot, naked, destitute as kings of people, and you see shepherds of sheep competing in building, and the slave woman gives birth to her mistress. The man said: You spoke the truth. Then he departed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the man. Umar said: We sought him but could not find him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Greatest; Jibril wanted to teach you your religion. No one narrated this hadith from Wabarah except Mujalid, nor from Mujalid except Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad; Abdullah ibn Umar is alone in narrating it."
"5198","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The well is of no liability, and the mine is of no liability. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Mujalid, nor from Mujalid except Ubaydah; Abdullah ibn Umar is alone in narrating it."
"5199","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Hayyan ibn Bishr al-Qadi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm nor reciprocal harm in Islam. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban except Ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Salamah is alone in narrating it."
"5200","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in Sad. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"5201","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumasi narrated to us, saying: Mu'ammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was resting at noon, and a son of Khadijah called Halah arrived, and she said: Halah, Halah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear Allah, O Aishah. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Hammad ibn Salamah, nor from Hammad except Mu'ammal; Nuh ibn Habib is alone in narrating it."
"5202","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The severest of people in punishment on the Day of Resurrection is an unjust ruler. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Abu Hafs al-Abbar."
"5203","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Makhlad ibn Khalid al-Sha'iri narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Murrah, from al-Musayyab, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When circumcision meets circumcision, or when circumcision touches circumcision, ghusl becomes obligatory. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Murrah except Abu Asim."
"5204","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Makhlad ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Khalid al-San'ani narrated to us, saying: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Abu Rashdin, from Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Ju'shum, that when he came from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would narrate to his people and teach them. A man said to him one day, as if jesting: Nothing remains for Suraqah except to teach you how to defecate. Suraqah said: When you go to relieve yourselves, avoid sitting in shaded places and on paths, take pebbles, clean yourselves upon your legs, and use odd numbers of stones."
"5205","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you belittle himself: that he sees a matter concerning which he should speak, yet does not speak of it; then he meets Allah having neglected that, and He says: What prevented you from speaking of it? He says: My Lord, I feared people. He says: I was more deserving to be feared. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"5206","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us, saying: Makhlad ibn Khalid al-Sha'iri narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jarrah narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Being killed is martyrdom, plague is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, burning is martyrdom, and the woman who dies in childbirth is a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nu'man ibn Rashid except Abu al-Jarrah; Rabah ibn Zayd is alone in narrating it."
"5207","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'shar al-Barra narrated to us, saying: Mayyah ibn Sari' narrated to me, saying: Mujahid narrated to me, that a Kufan man asked Ibn Abbas about the nabidh of jars. He placed his two fingers in his ears and said: May they become deaf if I lie against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard him saying: All intoxicants are forbidden - their black, red, green, and white. No one narrated this hadith from Mayyah ibn Sari' except Abu Ma'shar and Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani."
"5208","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that Ali was the bearer of the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Badr, and Qays ibn Sa'd was the bearer of Ali's banner, and the bearer of the banner of the Emigrants in all battles. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Abu Shaybah."
"5209","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, saying: I heard Thabit narrating, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Made beloved to me of this world are women and perfume, and the coolness of my eye is made in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Sallam Abu al-Mundhir."
"5210","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Warqa ibn Umar al-Yashkuri narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The lower garment of the believer is to mid-calf, and there is no sin upon him in what is between it and the ankles - or below the ankles; Allah does not look at one who drags his garment in pride. No one narrated this hadith from Warqa except Ali ibn al-Ja'd."
"5211","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn Abu Malik al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Abdullah al-Barrad, from Uqbah ibn Amr, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he bowed, straightened his back until if water were poured upon his back it would settle. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn."
"5212","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man following a bird and said: A devil following a devil. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, except Sharik; Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurarah is alone in narrating it. And Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"5213","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Jabir al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Maymun Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to sleep or eat while in janabah, would perform ablution as for prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah except Ibn Ulayyah; Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan is alone in narrating it."
"5214","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Jassas, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise; O Allah, I love them, so love them. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad al-Jassas except Ismail ibn Ulayyah and Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi; Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi is alone in narrating it from Ibn Ulayyah."
"5215","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Khasib al-Antaki narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward al-Makhzumi narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah saying: I heard Aishah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Three things I forbade you: visiting graves, sacrificial meats beyond three days, and drinking in pitched, green-glazed, and hollowed vessels. Now visit your brothers and greet them, for therein is a lesson; and sacrificial meats - eat of them and store; and every intoxicant is wine, and every wine is forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward except Muhammad ibn Abi al-Khasib."
"5216","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Imran Abu al-Nu'man al-Ammi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will emerge in this ummah a people whose mark is shaving; they pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the prey, then never return to it. No one narrated this hadith from Imran ibn Abi al-Nu'man except Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh."
"5217","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: al-Ala ibn Salamah al-Hudhali al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Shaybah Abu Qilabah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach leaning upon a palm trunk, resting his back against it. It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, Islam has spread, people have grown many, and delegations come to you from the horizons; if you ordered something made for you to be seen upon. He said to a man: Can you make the minbar? He said: Yes. He said: What is your name? He said: So-and-so. He said: You are not its maker. Then he called another and said: Can you make the minbar? He said: Yes. He said the same as he said to this one, and he said: Yes, if Allah wills. He said: What is your name? He said: Ibrahim. He said: Set about making it. When he made it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended it, and the trunk - the palm trunk - moaned like the moaning of a she-camel; the people of the mosque - or he said the people of Madinah - heard its voice. So he descended and embraced it, and it calmed. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, had I left it, it would have moaned until the Day of Resurrection, or it would have moaned as long as I left it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Shaybah Abu Qilabah."
"5218","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Abu Hafs al-Saffar Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Hilal al-Bariqi narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say concerning stray sheep? He said: For you, your brother, or the wolf. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say concerning hanging dates? He said: Its fine and its like with it, and lashes as deterrence; and when it is sheltered in the storehouse, whatever reaches the price of a shield entails cutting. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say concerning cattle pastured in the mountains? He said: Its fine and its like with it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say concerning lost property? He said: Whatever of it is in an inhabited village or on a frequented road, announce it for a year; if you find its owner, well, otherwise it is the wealth of Allah He gives to whom He wills; and in buried treasure is the fifth. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Asim ibn Hilal and Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan."
"5219","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah - raised - who said: No pilgrim ever became poor. It was said to Jabir: What is im'ar? He said: Becoming poor. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Muhammad ibn Zayd."
"5220","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Saj al-Harrani, from Sa'd ibn Tariq, from his father, who said: I said: O father, you prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and behind Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman - did they recite qunut in Fajr? He said: O my son, it is an innovation. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Saj except Sa'id ibn Salim."
"5221","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, saying: Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will fill your hands with non-Arabs, and they will become lions who do not flee; they will strike your necks and take your spoils. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus, and it is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr except with this chain."
"5222","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When dinner is served and the prayer is established, begin with dinner. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ayyub ibn Utbah."
"5223","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Layth ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the softest of shoulders in prayer, and there is no step greater in reward than a step a man takes to a gap in a row and fills it. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Layth ibn Hammad."
"5224","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not touch a woman, nor should a man touch a man in a single garment. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"5225","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Abu Hafs al-Saffar Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Waqid al-Saffar narrated to us, from a man of the people of Makkah called Salim, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: A book Allah wrote, in it are the names of the people of Paradise by their names and lineages, sealed upon them; none are added among them nor diminished from them until the Day of Resurrection. The companion of Paradise is sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the companion of the Fire is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire, whatever deed he does. The people of felicity may be led along the path of the people of wretchedness until it is said: How they resemble them, indeed they are of them, then felicity overtakes them and rescues them. And the people of wretchedness may be led along the path of the people of felicity until it is said: How they resemble them, indeed they are of them, then wretchedness overtakes them. Whoever Allah wrote as felicitous in the Mother of the Book will not be taken from this world until He employs him in a deed that makes him happy before his death, even for the time of milking a she-camel. Then he said: Deeds are by their endings, deeds are by their endings. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Hammad ibn Waqid alone narrated it."
"5226","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Hammad al-Attar al-Tarsusi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, saying: al-Azhar ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said to Ali ibn Abi Talib: O Abu Hasan, at times you witnessed and we were absent, and at times we witnessed and you were absent. Three things I ask you about: do you have knowledge of them? Ali said: What are they? He said: A man loves a man without having seen any good from him, and a man hates a man without having seen any evil from him. He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Souls in the air are arrayed troops that meet and sniff one another; those of them that recognize one another unite, and those that do not recognize one another differ. Umar said: One. And a man narrates a report then forgets it, then remembers it? Ali said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no heart but it has a cloud like the cloud of the moon; while the moon is shining, a cloud covers it and it darkens, then when it clears from it, it shines; and while a man is narrating, a cloud covers him and he forgets, then when it clears from him, he remembers. Umar said: Two. And he said: A man sees a dream, some of it true and some of it false? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no servant, male or female, who sleeps and sleeps heavily except that his soul is taken up to the Throne; the one that does not wake except at the Throne, that is the dream that is true, and the one that wakes below the Throne, that is the dream that is false. So Umar said: Three things I was seeking; praise be to Allah Who let me attain them before death. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra alone narrated it."
"5227","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbar narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'ammar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not intend gentleness for the people of a household except that He benefits them thereby, and He does not withhold it from them except that He harms them. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Yasar except Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'ammar, and he is Abu Tuwalah."
"5228","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbar narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: I do not like to spend a night except that I have a debt upon me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no servant who has a debt upon him which he is concerned about repaying except that there is help from Allah with him for it until he settles it from him, so I do not like that the help of Allah should leave me. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim except Ibn Mujabbar."
"5229","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Ya'la ibn Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Mas'ud. No one narrated this hadith from Ya'la ibn Muslim except Sufyan ibn Husayn; Abbad alone narrated it."
"5230","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Abu Ubaydah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr prayer: Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Abbad ibn al-Awwam alone narrated it."
"5231","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of al-thunya (an exception of unknown quantity) until it is known. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Sufyan ibn Husayn; Abbad ibn al-Awwam alone narrated it."
"5232","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Khusayf, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated, he would turn the insides of his palms toward his face. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Abbad ibn al-Awwam alone narrated it."
"5233","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Musawir, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah will surely admit into Paradise a believer whom the Fire had scorched, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah will surely forgive on the Day of Resurrection a forgiveness that has never crossed the heart of a human, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah will surely forgive on the Day of Resurrection a forgiveness that Iblis will stretch toward hoping it will reach him. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Musawir, and Sa'd Abu Ghaylan."
"5234","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man goes out for Hajj with wholesome (lawful) provision, and places his foot in the stirrup and calls out: Here I am, O Allah, here I am, a caller from heaven calls out to him: May you be welcomed and aided; your provision is lawful, your mount is lawful, and your Hajj is accepted and free of sin. And when he goes out with impure provision, and places his foot in the stirrup and calls out: Here I am, a caller from heaven calls out to him: No welcome for you and no aid; your provision is unlawful, your spending is unlawful, and your Hajj is not accepted."
"5235","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These wailing women will be made into two rows in Hellfire on the Day of Resurrection, a row on their right and a row on their left, and they will bark at the people of the Fire just as dogs bark. No one narrated these two hadiths from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Yamami."
"5236","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Shihab, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu Fazarah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits, whoever does not have them in him, then whatever besides that is forgiven for him, if Allah wills: whoever dies not associating anything with Allah, whoever has not been a sorcerer following sorcerers, and whoever has not harbored malice toward his brother. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn al-Asamm except Abu Fazarah, nor from Abu Fazarah except Layth; Abu Shihab alone narrated it."
"5237","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my chamber and my prayer place is a garden from the gardens of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn al-Hakam except Adi ibn al-Fadl; Sa'id ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"5238","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Abd Allah ibn al-Sa'ib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Arabs will reach the birthplaces of their forefathers, the places where wormwood and qaysum grow. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah except Ali ibn al-Hakam, nor from Ali except Adi ibn al-Fadl; Sa'id ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"5239","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Hakim, from Yusuf ibn Suhayb, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom the angels do not approach: the drunkard, the one scented with khaluq (a saffron-based perfume), and the one in a state of major impurity. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf ibn Suhayb except Abd Allah ibn Hakim, and he is Abu Bakr al-Dahiri; Sa'id ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"5240","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: When Ja'far ibn Abi Talib came from Abyssinia, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is the most amazing thing you saw there? He said: I saw a woman with a basket of food on her head; a horseman passed galloping and scattered it, so she sat gathering it, then turned to him and said: Woe to you on the day the King sets up His Footstool and takes for the oppressed from the oppressor. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, confirming her words: A nation will not be sanctified - or: How can a nation be sanctified - in which the weak cannot take his right from the strong without being made to falter? No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib except Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad and Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"5241","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Usamah, from Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I set out from him, he sent after me and said: Do you know why I sent for you? I sent because of striking (taking property); do not take anything except what you have been permitted, for it is misappropriation from the spoils, and whoever misappropriates will bring what he misappropriated on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated it from al-Mughirah ibn Shubayl except Dawud al-Awdi; Abu Usamah alone narrated it."
"5242","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Tarsusi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Kardam, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A house in which there are no dates, its people are hungry. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd al-Rahman ibn Kardam; Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays alone narrated it."
"5243","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heat is intense, cool down the prayer (delay it), for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hellfire. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt except Ayyub ibn Utbah."
"5244","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast."
"5245","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Mahdi ibn Hafs narrated to us, saying: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays Isha in congregation, and prays four rak'ahs before leaving the mosque, it will be like the equivalent of Laylat al-Qadr. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except by Muharib ibn Dithar, nor from Muharib except by Abu Hanifah; Ishaq al-Azraq alone narrated it."
"5246","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Layth ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the softest of shoulders in prayer, and no servant takes a step greater in reward than a step a man takes to a gap in the row and fills it."
"5247","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Saffar narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Sa'id al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Masruq, from A'ishah, who said: You were commanded to seek forgiveness for your predecessors but you insulted them; indeed I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This ummah will not perish until its last curses its first. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, nor from Isma'il except Ubayd ibn Sa'id; Yusuf al-Saffar alone narrated it."
"5248","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, saying: Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: Five things the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left, neither at home nor on travel: the mirror, the kohl container, the comb, the parting tool, and the siwak (tooth-stick). No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la."
"5249","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day besides the obligatory prayer, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise: two rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Zuhr, two rak'ahs before Asr, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, two rak'ahs after Isha, and two rak'ahs before Fajr. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah except Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani. And Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Abu Ishaq - and Fulayh ibn Sulayman from Suhayl from Abu Ishaq -: from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah."
"5250","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Shahrazuri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from his father, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go early in seeking knowledge, for I asked my Lord to bless my ummah in its early mornings, and to make that Thursday. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Ayyub ibn Suwayd; his son alone narrated it."
"5251","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: I entered upon Jabir ibn Abd Allah, and he led us in prayer in a single garment, and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in a single garment. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Qays; Abu Bilal alone narrated it."
"5252","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated to us, saying: Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was forbidden to pray behind those engaged in conversation and those asleep. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Shuja' ibn al-Walid; Sahl ibn Salih alone narrated it."
"5253","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rak'ahs before Fajr: Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Yazid ibn Harun; Sahl ibn Salih alone narrated it."
"5254","Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, saying: Abu Waki' al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant except that he has a reputation in heaven; if his reputation in heaven is good, it is set upon earth, and if his reputation in heaven is bad, it is set upon earth. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except al-Jarrah ibn Malih and Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"5255","Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawrah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: I did not fast twenty-nine days with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more often than I fasted thirty. This hadith is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain; Ishaq ibn Sa'id alone narrated it."
"5256","Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawrah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qur'an was sent down in seven modes. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"5257","Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawrah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Bujayr narrated to us, from Sayyar al-Shami, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will emerge in this ummah people with whips like the tails of cows; they go out in the morning in Allah's displeasure and return in the evening in His wrath. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Abd Allah ibn Bujayr alone narrated it."
"5258","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi' ibn Shahin narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, saying: Sallam ibn Abi Muti' narrated to us, saying: I heard Ma'mar narrating from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a distribution, giving some people and leaving others. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave so-and-so and withheld from so-and-so, though he is a believer? He said: Do not say: a believer; say: a Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Sallam ibn Abi Muti' except Abu al-Walid."
"5259","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi' ibn Shahin narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to me, saying: We were with Anas ibn Malik, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - when a man was brought for him to pray over - and he said: Is there a debt upon your companion? They said: Yes. He said: How will it benefit you that I pray over a man whose soul is held in his grave, his soul not ascending to heaven? If a man guaranteed his debt, I would stand and pray over him, for my prayer would benefit him. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Isa ibn Sadaqah alone narrated it."
"5260","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi' ibn Shahin narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prefer one over another in division, and hardly a day passed but he would visit all of us, receiving benefit from each wife without intercourse, until reaching the one whose day it was, and he would stay with her. And Sawdah bint Zam'ah said to him - when she aged and feared he would part from her: O Messenger of Allah, my day which I receive from you is for A'ishah, so he accepted that from her. And concerning her likes was revealed: And if a woman fears from her husband discord or neglect, the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"5261","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi' ibn Shahin narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Funeral prayer was performed over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for three days. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abd al-Rahman ibn Mushir; Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki alone narrated it."
"5262","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi' ibn Shahin narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, saying: Qurrah ibn Khalid al-Sadusi narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Ashajj Ashajj Abd al-Qays: In you are two traits Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal."
"5263","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abd Allah Abu al-Mughallis narrated to us, saying: Nuh ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: Habib ibn al-Harith came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who frequently commits sins? He said: Then repent to Allah, O Habib. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I repent then return? He said: Every time you sin, repent. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then my sins will be many? He said: Allah's pardon is greater than your sins, O Habib ibn al-Harith. This hadith is not narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah except with this chain; Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki alone narrated it."
"5264","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us, saying: Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn al-Harith, from Awf ibn Sulayman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the bearer of the Qur'an, when he deems its lawful lawful and its unlawful unlawful, is that he may intercede for ten of his household, all of whom deserved the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far ibn al-Harith except Salm ibn Salim; Isa ibn Salim alone narrated it."
"5265","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Sawwar al-Anbari narrated to us, saying: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, who said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turn grey? He said: I do not think there were in his head and beard fifteen white hairs; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch them with yellowness. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil except Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"5266","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Sayyar al-Yashkuri narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Shibl narrated to us, from Umm al-Nu'man bint Arqam, that she heard A'ishah, Mother of the Believers, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Those who love one another for Allah's sake will be upon a pillar of ruby, with a tent of hollow ruby sixty miles into the sky; in every direction therein are spouses the others do not know of. One of them will overlook the people of Paradise and fill the people of Paradise with light, until the people of Paradise say: What is this that has occurred? Some of them say to others: What is this light that has occurred? Some of them say to others: A man from those who loved one another for Allah's sake has overlooked you. This hadith is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain."
"5267","Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Turki narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Khuza'i narrated to us, saying: Uwayn ibn Amr al-Qaysi, brother of Rabah, narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a house crowded with people. He stood at the door, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked right and left and saw no place. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his cloak, folded it, then threw it to him and said: Sit upon it. So Jarir took it, embraced and kissed it, then returned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May Allah honor you, O Messenger of Allah, as you honored me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id al-Jurayri except Uwayn ibn Amr, nor from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah except al-Jurayri, nor from Yahya ibn Ya'mar except Abd Allah ibn Buraydah."
"5268","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Talhah al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies ill dies as a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except Yahya ibn Talhah."
"5269","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dharih, from Muslim ibn Nudhayr, from Ali, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every Prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr, son of my paternal aunt. No one narrated this hadith from al-Abbas ibn Dharih except Sharik."
"5270","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzaz narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me, my mother treated me with everything but I did not gain weight, so she fed me cucumber with fresh dates, and I gained weight like the best weight gain. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Zayd ibn al-Hubab; al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah alone narrated it."
"5271","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Bahili narrated to us, saying: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever does not find sandals - meaning: the one in ihram - let him wear leather socks, and let him cut them below the ankles. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Abd al-A'la, and Muhammad ibn Bakr."
"5272","Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Thawab al-Husri narrated to us, saying: Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, saying: Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah on earth are more than the number of pebbles or the number of rain. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Suwayd Abu Hatim, nor from Suwayd except Talut; Sa'id ibn Muhammad alone narrated it."
"5273","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hisham al-Sijzi al-Harbi narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we reach our women in Paradise? He said: A man will indeed reach a hundred virgins in a day. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Za'idah; Husayn ibn Ali alone narrated it."
"5274","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hisham al-Harbi narrated to us, saying: al-Fadl ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Karim ibn Rawh narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, from his father Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from his grandmother Umm Ayyash, who said: I used to pour ablution water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was standing and he was sitting."
"5275","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Harbi narrated to us, saying: al-Fadl ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Karim ibn Rawh narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from his grandmother Umm Ayyash, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I did not marry Uthman to Umm Kulthum except by revelation from heaven. These two hadiths are not narrated from Umm Ayyash except with this chain; Abd al-Karim ibn Rawh alone narrated them."
"5276","Muhammad ibn al-Nahrutiri narrated to us, Uthman Abd al-Karim ibn Abi Umayr al-Dihqan narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Amr al-Awza'i and Isa ibn Yunus narrated to me, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is trusted; O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except al-Walid; Abd al-Karim ibn Abi Umayr alone narrated it."
"5277","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Nahrutiri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows, for part of the excellence of prayer is straightening the row. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Bishr ibn al-Sari; Muhammad ibn Abi Umar alone narrated it."
"5278","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Nahrutiri narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah, from Arfajah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man afflicted with a chronic ailment and prostrated, and that Abu Bakr received a victory and prostrated, and that Umar received a victory and prostrated. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Hafs ibn Ghiyath; Dawud ibn Rashid alone narrated it."
"5279","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Abu Sa'id al-Shaqari narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Jassas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you removes his sandals in prayer, let him not remove them in front of him lest he face them, nor behind him lest his Muslim brother face them, but let him place them between his feet. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jassas except Abu Sa'id al-Shaqari; Ali ibn al-Ja'd alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except with this chain."
"5280","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Spending in Hajj is like spending in the path of Allah: a dirham for seven hundred. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Musa ibn A'yan. And others narrated it from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Harb ibn Zuhayr, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father."
"5281","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend and chosen one (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three things and forbade me from three: he commanded me with the two rak'ahs of Duha, not to sleep except upon witr, and fasting three days of every month; and he forbade me: when I prostrate, from squatting like the squatting of a monkey, or pecking like the pecking of a crow, or turning like the turning of a fox. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except Habib ibn Abi Thabit, nor from Habib except Layth, nor from Layth except Musa ibn A'yan; al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"5282","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Bakr ibn Khunays, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, who said: A ruqyah for fever was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Present it to me. So they presented it to him: In the name of Allah, a horned wound, sea salt, qafta. He said: These are covenants Sulayman (peace be upon him) took upon pests; I see no harm in it. He said: A man was stung - while he was with Alqamah - and he treated him with it, and it was as if he was released from bonds. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ma'shar except Isma'il ibn Muslim, nor from Isma'il except Zayd ibn Bakr; Musa ibn A'yan alone narrated it."
"5283","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Bakr ibn Khunays, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Sha'bi, from Malik al-Ashtar, who said: I entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib and said: O Commander of the Believers, when we leave you we hear reports attributed to you that we do not hear from you; did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrust to you anything besides the Book of Allah? He said: No, except what is in this sheet. Then he called his slave girl and she brought him the sheet, and in it was: Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah sacred, and I declare Madinah sacred; its thorns are not to be cut nor its game to be startled. Whoever commits a crime therein or shelters a criminal, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. The believers are one hand against others; the lowest of them grants protection on their behalf. A believer is not killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, nor from al-Hajjaj except Zayd ibn Bakr; Musa ibn A'yan alone narrated it."
"5284","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to call the Farewell Hajj: the Hajj of Islam. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Musa ibn A'yan."
"5285","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Kurayz - and he was a companion of Umm al-Darda - raising the hadith to Umm al-Darda, Umm al-Darda raising it to Abu al-Darda, Abu al-Darda raising it, who said: There are no two men who love each other for Allah's sake in each other's absence except that the more beloved of them to Allah is the one with stronger love for his companion. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far ibn Burqan except Musa ibn A'yan."
"5286","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ma'mar ibn Rashid, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Fudayl al-Raqashi, from Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani, that he asked him about drinks, and he said: Shall I not narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He forbade dubba (hollowed gourds), hantam (green and white jars), muqayyar, and muzaffat (pitch-coated vessels). I said: What is hantam? He said: Green and white. I said: What is muqayyar? He said: Everything coated with tar, whether a waterskin or otherwise. No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Ma'mar, nor from Ma'mar except Musa ibn A'yan."
"5287","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one night in Ramadan: O A'ishah, spread a mat for me at your door. So I did, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to it, and those in the mosque gathered to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them. The next night the mosque was shaking and full of people in the evening, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and prayed with them the last Isha, then returned while the people were in the mosque, and said: O A'ishah, what is the matter with the people? I said: O Messenger of Allah, they heard of your prayer last night and gathered for you to pray with them. He said: Lift your mat, O A'ishah. She said: So I did, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained until the dawn prayer, and prayed with the people, then turned to them with his face, then said: O people, indeed your place was not hidden from me, and I did not spend the night, praise be to Allah, heedless, but I feared it would be made obligatory upon you, so take up of deeds what you can bear, for Allah Almighty does not tire until you tire. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani alone narrated it."
"5288","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah informed me, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan al-Asadiyyah - sister of Ukkashah ibn Mihsan, and she was among the first Muhajir women who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Upon you is this Indian aloeswood, for in it is healing from seven ailments, among them pleurisy."
"5289","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying about black seed: Upon you is this black grain, for in it is healing from everything except death, meaning death."
"5290","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, who said: Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Maghrib, and men from Banu Salamah would pray with him, then return to Banu Salamah while still seeing the places where arrows landed. No one narrated these hadiths from Ishaq except Musa ibn A'yan."
"5291","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath while lying in it, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Ibn Ulathah; Musa ibn A'yan alone narrated it."
"5292","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Rashid, from a man kunya'd Abu Ubayd, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty is indeed shy toward a grey-haired Muslim, when he is upright and devoted to the Sunnah, to ask Allah and He not give him. No one narrated this hadith from Salih ibn Rashid except Musa ibn A'yan, and Abu Ubayd - in my view - is Abu Ubayd, the companion of Sulayman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan."
"5293","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a night journey, and he said: Who is this? I said: I am al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah. He said: Hold on for me, so I held his she-camel for him, and he went until I could not see him, then returned and I performed his ablution for him. He bared his forearms, but the sleeve of the cloak was tight, so he brought his hands out from under it and performed ablution: he washed his hands, face, and forearms, wiped his head, and wiped over his leather socks. I said: Shall I not remove your leather socks, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I put them on while pure. No one perfected this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Musa ibn A'yan; al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman alone narrated it. And al-Mu'afa also narrated it from al-Qasim, from Ma'n, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, without mentioning Urwah ibn al-Mughirah."
"5294","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Bara narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Mujalid, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs with which we hunt? He said: Look at these trained beasts of prey; teach them from what Allah taught you, and eat from what they hold for you. What it kills without eating from it, eat from it, and what it kills and eats from it, do not eat from it. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if other dogs mix with them? He said: He forbade that."
"5295","Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Hudbah ibn al-Minhal, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing between a man and disbelief and polytheism except abandoning prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Hudbah ibn al-Minhal except Abu Hammam."
"5296","Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah ibn al-Birind narrated to us, saying: Attab ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a group of Banu Hashim: Is there anyone with you from other than you? They said: No, except our nephew - or our freedman - so he said: When one of you is struck by worry or hardship, let him say: Allah, Allah, my Lord; I associate nothing with Him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except Attab ibn Harb; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah alone narrated it."
"5297","Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Uruzzi narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Hilal al-Bariqi narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar - raising it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: The best of you are the softest of shoulders in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Asim ibn Hilal."
"5298","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Barbari narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a man who hears my saying, retains it, then conveys it; for often one conveyed retains more than the hearer. Three things over which the heart of a Muslim man does not harbor deceit: sincerity of deed for Allah, sincere counsel to Muslim rulers, and adhering to their community, for their call encompasses those behind them. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi; Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih alone narrated it."
"5299","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abi al-Attaf narrated to me, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Hurayrah, learn the laws of inheritance, for it is half of knowledge, and it will be forgotten, and it is the first thing taken from my ummah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abi al-Attaf."
"5300","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not raise your gazes to the sky lest your sights be snatched - meaning: in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father except Yunus; Sulayman ibn Bilal alone narrated it."
"5301","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a silver ring on his right hand, with an Abyssinian stone, placing its stone inside his palm. In this hadith, no one said, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: on his right hand, except Yunus, and none narrated it from Yunus except Sulayman ibn Bilal and Talhah ibn Yahya al-Laythi."
"5302","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, saying: Qays Abu Umarah narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever visits a sick person remains in mercy until, when he sits with him, he immerses in it; and when he rises from him, he continues wading in it until he returns whence he came. And whoever consoles his believing brother over a calamity, Allah will clothe him with garments of honor on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Amr ibn Hazm except with this chain; Ibn Abi Uways alone narrated it."
"5303","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, Musa ibn Shaybah al-Ansari - of the descendants of Ka'b ibn Malik - narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Shaybah al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Ibn Kulayb narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Jabir and Mahmud ibn Jabir, both saying: We went out on the day Hubaysh ibn Duljah entered Madinah a year after al-Harrah; he entered Madinah to the height of the minbar, and the people panicked, so we went out with Jabir in al-Harrah while his sight had gone, stones striking him, and he said: May Allah frighten whoever frightened the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying it twice - or thrice - before we asked him. We said: O father, who frightened the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever frightens the Ansar has frightened what is between these two sides of mine. This hadith is not narrated from Muhammad and Mahmud, sons of Jabir, except with this chain; Musa ibn Shaybah alone narrated it."
"5304","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told while at al-Aqiq: You are in the blessed valley, or in a blessed plain."
"5305","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: My maternal uncle Uthman ibn Maz'un sent me to bring him a quilt, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought his permission while he was at the Trench, and he permitted me, and said: Whoever you meet of them, tell them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to return. That was in severe cold. So I went out and met the people and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to return. He said: By Allah, not even two or one of them turned to me."
"5306","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said to his brother Zayd ibn al-Khattab on the day of Uhud: Take this armor of mine, O brother. He said to him: I desire from martyrdom the same as you desire, so they both left it. No one narrated these hadiths from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi."
"5307","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that an army gained food and honey as spoils in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no fifth was taken from them. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Abu Damrah."
"5308","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Harb ibn Qays, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves that His concessions be acted upon just as He dislikes that His disobedience be committed. None put Harb ibn Qays in this hadith between Musa ibn Uqbah and Nafi' except al-Darawardi."
"5309","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Abu Mus'ab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Zurarah ibn Mus'ab ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, saying: al-Hakam ibn Sa'id al-Sa'idi narrated to us, from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in the end of time a people who deny predestination; indeed those are the Magians of this ummah: if they fall ill do not visit them, and if they die do not attend them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ju'ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman except al-Hakam; Abu Mus'ab alone narrated it."
"5310","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh narrated to us, saying: Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, saying: Abu Thabit Imran ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Malawayh, freedman of Jabir ibn Abd Allah, narrated to me, saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every fanged beast of prey, and every taloned bird. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Malawayh, freedman of Jabir, except Imran ibn Abd al-Aziz; Abu Mus'ab alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"5311","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you enters upon his Muslim brother and he feeds him food, let him eat from his food and not ask about it; and if he gives him drink, let him drink from his drink and not ask about it. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Muslim ibn Khalid."
"5312","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Sharik and Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him praying in a single garment wrapped around him, and I ate with him, and he said: Mention Allah's name over it, eat with your right, and eat from what is near you. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik and Mubarak ibn Fadalah except Ali ibn al-Ja'd."
"5313","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Matar al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they praised him with evil, yet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) welcomed him. When he turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people in station before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is he whom people fear for his evil. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit al-Bunani except Uthman ibn Matar, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"5314","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, saying: Abu Salim - or he said: Salim, freedman of al-Mahri - narrated to me, that he heard A'ishah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Woe to the heels from the Fire. None put Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman in the chain of this hadith between Yahya ibn Abi Kathir and Salim, freedman of al-Mahri - and he is the freedman of al-Nasriyyin - except Ikrimah ibn Ammar, nor from Ikrimah except Umar ibn Yunus; Abu Ubayd alone narrated it."
"5315","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything of the amusement of this world is false except three: your shooting with your bow, your training your horse, and your playing with your wife, for they are from the truth. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is dearer to me. And Allah Almighty indeed admits by a single arrow three into Paradise: its maker seeking reward therein, the one who supplies it, and the one who shoots it. And Allah Almighty indeed admits by a morsel of bread, a handful of dates, and the like of what the poor benefit from, three into Paradise: the master of the house who commands it, the wife who prepares it, and the servant who hands it to the poor. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Praise be to Allah Who did not forget our servants."
"5316","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Sabbah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, saying: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Raja ibn Haywah and Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The poor Muslims came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the wealthy have gone with the ranks; they pray as we pray, fast as we fast, and perform Hajj as we perform Hajj, and they have surplus wealth from which they give charity, and we have nothing to give. He said: Shall I not guide you to a matter which, if you do it, you will catch up with those who preceded you, and none after you will catch up with you except one who does like what you do? You glorify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times. That reached the rich, so they said the same as they said, and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: That is Allah's bounty He gives to whom He wills."
"5317","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, saying: Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, saying: Dimam ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan - may Allah have mercy on him - who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: After me there will be leaders who speak upon their pulpits and their words are not refuted; they plunge into the Fire as monkeys plunge. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Qabil except Dimam ibn Isma'il."
"5318","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, saying: Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Iskandarani narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies guarding the frontier in Allah's path, his provision from Paradise continues for him, his deed grows for him until the Day of Resurrection, and he is protected from the two tempters of the grave. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except his son Abd al-Rahman; Hani ibn al-Mutawakkil alone narrated it."
"5319","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Narsi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: I read to Abu Umar Hafs ibn Umar al-Duri al-Muqri, from Abu Muhammad al-Yazidi, who said: Abu Amr ibn al-Ala narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: How can it be that he may not misappropriate? When it was allowed for him to be killed? Allah Blessed and Exalted said: And they kill the Prophets without right, but the hypocrites accused the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding something, so Allah Almighty revealed: It is not for a Prophet to misappropriate. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amr ibn al-Ala except Abu Muhammad al-Yazidi; Abu Umar al-Duri alone narrated it."
"5320","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Narsi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Hisham al-Mada'ini narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Lahiq al-Mada'ini narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, who said: I was traveling on a donkey of mine, and I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I moved to the rear of the donkey and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, ride. He said: You are more entitled to the front of your donkey. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the donkey is yours. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode at its front, and I rode at its rear."
"5321","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Narsi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Hisham ibn Bahram al-Mada'ini narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Lahiq al-Mada'ini narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, who said: While I was in a garden of Madinah's gardens, I caught sight of a woman, and I had no concern but her until she passed me, then I followed her with my gaze until I came alongside the wall, then I turned and it struck my face and bloodied me. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am ruined. He said: And what is that, O Abu Tamimah? So I told him, and he said: When Allah Almighty intends good for a servant, He hastens the punishment of his sin in this world, and our Lord Blessed and Exalted is more generous than to punish for a sin twice. No one narrated these two hadiths from Asim al-Ahwal except Hisham ibn Lahiq."
"5322","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Uruzzi narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Tammam narrated to us, saying: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Ali ibn Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you marry her, return our daughter to us. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Abd Allah ibn Tammam; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Uruzzi alone narrated it."
"5323","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Zurarah al-Hadathi narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Uthman al-Balawi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather Asim ibn Adi, who said: My brother and I bought a hundred shares of Khaybar's shares, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Two ravenous wolves left among sheep whose owner neglected them are no more corrupting to them than a Muslim's seeking wealth and honor is to his religion. This hadith is not narrated from Asim ibn Adi except with this chain; Isa ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"5324","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Aban al-Mukattib, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawlah bint Qays, that Hamzah and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) discussed the world, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is green and sweet; whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it, and many a one who plunges into Allah's wealth and His Messenger's wealth will have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Aban al-Mukattib except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"5325","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated in the refuse heap of the sons of so-and-so, and said: O Mughirah, do you have water? I said: Yes, a waterskin of water. And upon him was a Syrian cloak with narrow sleeves. So he performed ablution and wiped over his feet and over his leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Janab except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"5326","Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, saying: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj brought a bone while circumambulating the House, or on the day of sacrifice, and he bit off a piece from it, and did not perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ayyub ibn Utbah; Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid alone narrated it."
"5327","Muhammad ibn al-Sari narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad, Sabalan, narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out for Hajj and dies, the reward of the pilgrim is written for him until the Day of Resurrection; and whoever goes out for Umrah and dies, the reward of the one performing Umrah is written for him until the Day of Resurrection; and whoever goes out as a warrior and dies, the reward of the warrior is written for him until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi except Jamil ibn Abi Maymunah, nor from Jamil except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Abu Mu'awiyah alone narrated it."
"5328","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, saying: Maslamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, that Abd Allah ibn Umar said: What do you say to your rulers when you enter upon them? They said: We say to them what they desire. He said: And when you leave them, what do you say? They said: We say what they do not desire. He said: This is what we used to count as hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Maslamah ibn Alqamah; al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah alone narrated it."
"5329","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Abbadi al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying alone behind the rows and said: Repeat the prayer. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Abbadi alone narrated it."
"5330","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, saying: al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees one afflicted and says: Praise be to Allah Who saved me from what He afflicted you with, and favored me over many of those He created, that affliction will not strike him. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, nor from al-Mughirah except Shababah; Zakariyya ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"5331","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Abbadi narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What enables you to attain Paradise is feeding food and sweetening speech. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Husayn except Abd Allah ibn Dawud; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Abbadi alone narrated it."
"5332","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Jumay' narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah - raising it - who said: Do you know which charity is best? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Al-manih: that one grants a dirham, or the back of a mount. No one narrated this hadith from Simak ibn Harb except Hafs ibn Jumay'; Umar ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"5333","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Isa ibn Zadham narrated to us, saying: Khalid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Abu Hasin, from Abu Zibyan, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wiping over leather socks is for the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Khalid ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"5334","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qassas narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Malik ibn Yukhamir, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am a guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest part of Paradise, for whoever abandons argument though he is right, abandons lying though jesting, and has good character. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh ibn al-Qasim except Isa ibn Shu'ayb; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn alone narrated it."
"5335","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Mu'min al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Umar ibn Dharr, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reaches Arafah before the sun rises has reached Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Dharr except Ubayd ibn Aqil."
"5336","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Suda'i narrated to us, saying: Jumay' ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Rashid, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion, for there is no religion but Yours. I said: O Messenger of Allah, are the hearts of servants in Allah's Hand? He said: Yes, between two fingers of Allah's fingers; when He wills to turn the heart of a servant, He turns it. No one narrated this hadith from Abbad ibn Rashid except Jumay' ibn Muhammad; al-Suda'i alone narrated it."
"5337","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Shuja' al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Waki' narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Abu Qays, I think from Hudhayl, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Part of the Sunnah is prayer in the cemetery. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Waki'."
"5338","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Ali al-Sayrafi narrated to us, saying: al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad al-Ta'i narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Sari' narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching his beard in prayer. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except with this chain; Amr ibn Ali alone narrated it."
"5339","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, saying: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Here I am for Umrah and Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman except his son al-Mu'tamir; Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi alone narrated it."
"5340","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Haytham al-Abdi al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Kathir Abu Ghassan al-Anbari narrated to us, saying: Za'idah ibn Abi al-Ruqad narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who approaches his wife in her rear, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is the lesser sodomy. No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Za'idah ibn Abi al-Ruqad; Yahya ibn Kathir alone narrated it."
"5341","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Salt narrated to us, saying: My uncle Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zur'ah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no Prophet after me. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Abi Zur'ah except Ali ibn Abis, nor from Ali except Muhammad ibn al-Salt; his nephew Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj alone narrated it."
"5342","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: I found in my grandfather's book in his handwriting: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hani al-Nakha'i narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, Mus'ab ibn Sulaym, and Harmalah ibn Qays informed us, from Rabah ibn al-Harith, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am in Paradise, and Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman, Sa'd, and Sa'id ibn Zayd. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, Mus'ab ibn Sulaym, and Harmalah ibn Qays except Abu Nu'aym al-Nakha'i; Ibn Abi Khaythamah alone narrated it."
"5343","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Ali al-Sayrafi narrated to us, saying: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from A'ishah, who said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, and I would not undo my hair."
"5344","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Ja'far ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, he said: Call for a sheet and ink for me, I will write for you a book after which you will never go astray. So we disliked that intensely. Then he said: Call for a sheet for me, I will write for you a book after which you will never go astray. The women said from behind the curtain: Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says? I said: You are the companions of Yusuf; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is ill, you squeeze your eyes, and when he recovers, you ride his neck. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them? For they are better than you."
"5345","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Ja'far ibn Ibrahim al-Ja'fari narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, I and Abu Bakr came to Ali, and we said: What do you say about what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left? He said: We are the most entitled of people to the Messenger of Allah and to what he left. He said: I said: And that in Khaybar? He said: And that in Khaybar. I said: And that in Fadak? He said: And that in Fadak. I said: By Allah, until you cut our necks with saws, no. No one narrated these two hadiths from Zayd ibn Aslam except Hisham ibn Sa'd, nor from Hisham except Musa ibn Ja'far al-Ja'fari; Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Attar alone narrated them."
"5346","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, that Jibril - peace be upon him - came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieving, not raising his head. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why do I see you, O Jibril, grieving? He said: I saw a blast of Hellfire, and my soul has not returned to me since. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Ali ibn Abd Allah; Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf alone narrated it."
"5347","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, saying: al-Mughirah Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Aban ibn al-Qasim, from al-Harith al-A'war, who said: I entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, and he said: Shall I not teach you a supplication the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me? I said: Yes. He said: Say: O Allah, open the hearings of my heart to Your remembrance, grant me obedience to You and obedience to Your Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and deeds by Your Book. This hadith is not narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except with this chain; Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam alone narrated it."
"5348","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Hafs al-Tawmani narrated to us, saying: Fudalah ibn Husayn al-Attar narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Na'amah narrated to us, saying: Utbah ibn Ghazwan addressed us, saying: This world has announced its parting and turned away swiftly, and nothing remains of it but a remnant like the remnant of a vessel. I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten days, with no food but the leaves of basham and the thorns of qatad until our mouths were ulcerated. It has reached me that a stone is cast from the edge of Hellfire, falling in it seventy years without reaching its bottom. It has reached me that between the two door-leaves of Paradise is a journey of seven hundred years, and a day will come upon it when it is crowded with throngs. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Na'amah except Fudalah ibn Husayn."
"5349","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari narrated to us, that Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to him, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intercession is for whoever says: There is no god but Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah except Hafs al-Minqari, nor from Hafs except Rawh ibn Ata; Wahb ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"5350","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Anbari narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from al-Muhajir Abu Makhlad, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, both saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought garments, so he sent to Umar a garment. Umar came carrying his garment on his hands and said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent me this silk garment, though you said about it what you said? He said: I did not send it to you to wear it, but sell it and benefit from its price. No one narrated this hadith from al-Muhajir except Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi."
"5351","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: al-Qasim ibn Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib ibn Sharik narrated to us, saying: al-Haytham ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Tamim ibn Tarafah narrated to us, from his father, from Adi ibn Hatim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes in an orphan, his own or another's, until Allah enriches him from him, Paradise becomes due for him. Abd Allah ibn Tamim ibn Tarafah did not narrate any hadith with a chain besides this, and this hadith is not narrated from Adi ibn Hatim except with this chain; al-Qasim ibn Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib ibn Sharik alone narrated it."
"5352","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Suda'i narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Hayyan al-Taymi narrating, from Abu Zur'ah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sheep are among the beasts of Paradise, so wipe their mucus and pray in their resting places. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hayyan except Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah."
"5353","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Suhayb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunya Abu Yahya. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Amr ibn Asim."
"5354","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Idris ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, saying: al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Zurayq, from Abu Ishaq, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Mas'ud, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I stay behind from Fajr prayer because of how long our imam prolongs it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and addressed the people, saying: Among you are those who repel; when you lead people, be brief, for among them are the elderly and those in need. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq al-Sabi'i except Ammar ibn Zurayq, nor from Ammar except Abu al-Jawwab; Idris ibn al-Hakam alone narrated it, and the well-known version is from the hadith of Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays."
"5355","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Hatim ibn Bakr ibn Ghaylan al-Quta'i narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Huna'i narrated to us, saying: Mujja'ah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Dhakwan Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and from Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Abu Hurayrah, they forbade currency exchange; two of them said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade currency exchange. No one narrated this hadith from Mujja'ah ibn al-Zubayr except Muhammad ibn Abbad; Hatim ibn Bakr alone narrated it."
"5356","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Ghassan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon the fitrah. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except al-Harith ibn Ghassan; Umar ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"5357","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Amr al-Hadhdha al-Madini narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the believer falls ill, Allah purifies him of sins just as the bellows purifies the dross of iron. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ibn Abi Dhi'b, nor from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Abd Allah ibn Nafi'; Muslim ibn Amr alone narrated it."
"5358","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats or drinks forgetfully in Ramadan, there is no makeup upon him, nor expiation. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except al-Ansari; Muhammad ibn Marzuq alone narrated it."
"5359","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Umar al-Ubulli narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, who said: I witnessed Madinah with Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas in it, and a man came to its governor and testified before him to sighting the Ramadan crescent. Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas asked about his testimony, then ordered him to accept it, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted the testimony of a single man for sighting the Ramadan crescent, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not accept testimony for breaking the fast except the testimony of two men."
"5360","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Umar al-Ubulli narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I indeed intended to send teachers among people, as Isa son of Maryam sent the disciples to the Children of Israel. It was said to him: What about Abu Bakr and Umar, will you not send them? He said: I cannot do without them; they are to the religion as the head is to the body. No one narrated these two hadiths from Mis'ar except Hafs."
"5361","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Shadhan narrated to us, saying: al-Hurr ibn Malik al-Anbari narrated to us, saying: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, I think from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The children of polytheists are servants of the people of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak ibn Fadalah except al-Hurr ibn Malik."
"5362","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Karim ibn Abi Abd al-Karim narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from al-Husayn ibn Waqid, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever withholds grapes during harvest days to sell them to a Jew or Christian, or to one who makes them wine, has plunged into the Fire knowingly. This hadith is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi alone narrated it."
"5363","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, Shababah narrated to us, from Warqa ibn Umar, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard al-Hajjaj delivering a sermon, and he mentioned something I disapproved of, so I remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It is not fitting for a believer to humiliate himself. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he humiliate himself? He said: He exposes himself to trial he cannot bear. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Abd al-Karim; Warqa alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"5364","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Darir narrated to us, Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Safiyyah, made freeing her her dowry, and served people hays on a leather mat as a wedding feast. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir except Warqa, nor from Warqa except Shababah; Zakariyya ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"5365","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Salt al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: My uncle Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Hasin, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Mas'ud or another, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an? They said: Who can do that? He said: Can one of you not recite: Say: He is Allah, the One, for it equals a third of the Qur'an. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hasin except Qays, nor from Qays except Ibn al-Salt; his nephew Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj alone narrated it."
"5366","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr, the companion of Ali ibn al-Madini, narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Ashath al-Sulami narrated to us: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Unays al-Ansari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed I shall intercede on the Day of Resurrection for everything upon the face of the earth, whether stone or clay. This hadith is not narrated from Unays al-Ansari except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Amr, known as al-Qillawri, a Basran, was alone in narrating it. Unays al-Ansari who narrated this hadith is, in my view, and Allah knows best, Unays al-Bayadi of Banu Bayada; he is mentioned in the books of military expeditions."
"5367","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna narrated to us: Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari narrated to us that Ata ibn Abi Maymuna reported to him, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding a young goat he came upon: Do you see that this was worthless to its owners when they threw it away? They said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The world is more insignificant to Allah than this was to its owners when they threw it away. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam was alone in narrating it."
"5368","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran al-Abidi al-Makki narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted is He, descends every night when a third of the night remains, and says: Who supplicates to Me so that I may answer him; who asks of Me so that I may give him; who seeks My forgiveness so that I may forgive him, until dawn rises. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, except Ibrahim ibn Sad. Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, Mamar, Malik, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamza, Sufyan ibn Uyayna and others among the companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Abdullah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayra."
"5369","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran al-Abidi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man among those before you wronged himself greatly, and when death came to him he said to his family: When I die, burn me, then grind me, then scatter me in the wind over the sea. They did that to him. Then Allah, majestic is His remembrance, said to the wind: Gather what is in you, and there he was, standing. He said: What moved you to do what you did? He said: Fear of You, O Lord. He said: Then I have forgiven you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, except Ibrahim ibn Sad. The companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayra."
"5370","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us: Said ibn al-Fadl al-Qurashi narrated to us: Said ibn Iyas al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah al-Anazi, from Maqil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a slave to set him free should not stipulate the freeing as a condition binding its sellers, for his contract remains one of bondage. No one narrated this hadith in raised form from Said al-Jurayri except Said ibn al-Fadl. Yazid ibn Zuray, Khalid al-Tahhan and others narrated it from Said al-Jurayri as the stopped statement of Maqil ibn Yasar."
"5371","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Uthman al-Kurayzi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not proper for a learned man to remain silent about his knowledge, nor is it proper for an ignorant man to remain silent about his ignorance. Allah, majestic is His remembrance, said: So ask the people of remembrance if you do not know. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; al-Ansari was alone in narrating it."
"5372","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Basri narrated to us: Abu Hafs al-Abdi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever performs ablution fully in severe cold shall have a double share of reward. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Abu Hafs al-Abdi, whose name is Umar ibn Hafs."
"5373","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abi Mamar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Bishr, from Shurayh ibn Hani, who said: I asked Aisha about wiping over the leather socks, and she said: Go to Ali ibn Abi Talib, for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I went to him and asked him. He said: We used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would not remove our socks for three days and their nights, and for the resident one day and one night. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira, a Kufan shaykh who settled in Egypt."
"5374","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Ansari narrated to us: Mansur ibn Ikrima narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Qatada, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: No, but Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, dyed with henna and katam. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Qatada, except Mansur ibn Ikrima. Muhammad ibn Salama al-Harrani narrated it from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: I asked Anas, and he mentioned something similar."
"5375","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Sayyar al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abu Hamza al-Sukkari narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the emigration, I would be a man of the Ansar. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Abu Hamza al-Sukkari."
"5376","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna narrated to us: Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari narrated to us that Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa reported to him, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intercession is for whoever says: There is no god but Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Hafs al-Minqari except Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna; Wahb ibn Yahya was alone in narrating it."
"5377","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bishr al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Salama ibn Raja narrated to us: Misar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to prostrate upon seven: upon the forehead, the two hands, the two knees, and the two feet. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Salama ibn Raja and al-Mushmail ibn Milhan."
"5378","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Shabba ibn Ubayda al-Numayri narrated to us: Maslama ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Marzuq Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loses his two precious things, his eyes, and remains patient seeking reward, I am not content with any reward for him less than Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Marzuq Abu Bakr, nor from Marzuq except Maslama; Umar ibn Shabba was alone in narrating it."
"5379","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Tawba narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq and Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqba, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying something good or conveying something good. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Atiq except Hammad ibn Zayd, and none narrated it from Hammad ibn Zayd except Yunus ibn Muhammad."
"5380","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ward narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Abu Amr, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra saw people praying the forenoon prayer and said: My father informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away along with most of his companions, and they did not pray this prayer. This Abu Amr is, in my view, Abu Amr ibn al-Ala who narrated this hadith; none narrated it from him except Adi ibn al-Fadl. Ward ibn Abdullah was alone in narrating it."
"5381","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Khaqan al-Nahwi narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, from Kharija ibn Musab, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted is He, laughs at the despair and hopelessness of His servants, while His mercy is near to them. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Kharija ibn Musab, and it is not narrated from Aisha except with this chain."
"5382","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Jamila, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Carry out the prescribed punishments upon those whom your right hands possess. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Sharik; Abu al-Jawwab was alone in narrating it. If Abu al-Jawwab preserved it correctly, it is a strange hadith of Ata ibn al-Saib, for people narrated it from Sharik, from Abd al-Ala al-Thalabi, and from Ibn Abi Jamila, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"5383","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Aban ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Ayyub al-Bajali narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ziyad al-Thaqafi, from Anas, who said: There was a woman in Medina who was a perfume seller, and he mentioned the hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the virtue of a man having intercourse with his wife. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except Jarir ibn Ayyub."
"5384","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sudran al-Salami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: Some people were at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day disputing about the Quran. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with his face changed, and said: O people, by this the nations perished. The Quran confirms one part of it with another, so do not deny one part of it by means of another. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar. Mamar narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather."
"5385","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No charity is due from a man for his slave or his horse. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih except Uthman ibn Uthman al-Ghatafani."
"5386","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umara al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Makhrama ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from his father, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats food should not wipe his hand until he licks his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food blessing is placed for him. No one narrated this hadith from Busr ibn Said except Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj; his son Makhrama was alone in narrating it."
"5387","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umara al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Makhrama ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Abdullah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayra, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate food he would lick his fingers, and he said: Licking the bowl is a blessing. No one narrated this hadith from al-Agharr except Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj; Makhrama was alone in narrating it."
"5388","Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri, of the descendants of Abdullah ibn Busr, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awzai reported to me, he said: I passed by your grandfather Abd al-Wahid ibn Abdullah ibn Busr while I was on a campaign and he was governor over Hims, and he said to me: O Abu Amr, shall I not report to you a hadith that will delight you; by Allah, I would sometimes conceal it from the rulers? I said: Yes. He said: My father Abdullah ibn Busr reported to me, he said: While we were one day sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he came out to us with his face radiant and beaming. We stood up before him and said: May Allah delight you, O Messenger of Allah; we are indeed delighted by what we see of the radiance of your face. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me just now and gave me glad tidings that Allah has granted me intercession; it is for my community, for the sinful and heavily burdened. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Abd al-Wahid al-Nasri; Shadhan was alone in narrating it."
"5389","Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Shuja al-Sakuni narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to grant additional spoils in his military expeditions. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah except Ismail ibn Ayyash."
"5390","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umara narrated to us, he said: Makhrama ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from his father, from Zuhra ibn Mabad, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he ate he would say: Praise be to Allah who fed and gave drink, made it easy to swallow, and made for it an exit."
"5391","Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ward ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: my father reported to me, from Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver two sermons, sitting between them. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Adi ibn al-Fadl; Ward ibn Abdullah was alone in narrating it."
"5392","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ward ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Uthman al-Batti, from Muhammad ibn al-Qasim, from Abu Hurayra, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to supplicate for a people or against a people, he performed qunut. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman al-Batti except Adi ibn al-Fadl; Ward ibn Abdullah was alone in narrating it."
"5393","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Umar ibn Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran reported to me, he said: my father reported to me, from his father Amr ibn Maymun, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: I remember us at Fajj al-Rawha, on a campaign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) undertook; Umar saw me and supplicated for me with supplications for which the world and all it contains would not delight me as much. This hadith is not narrated from Maymun except with this chain."
"5394","Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, who said: al-Zuhri reported to me, from Urwa, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sets out in this direction for Hajj or Umra and dies shall neither be exposed for judgment nor reckoned, and it shall be said to him: Enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Jafar ibn Burqan; Husayn al-Jufi was alone in narrating it."
"5395","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad ibn Thawab al-Husri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he missed the Friday prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to give a dinar in charity. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; al-Ansari was alone in narrating it. What is well known is from the hadith of Samura ibn Jundub."
"5396","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sawada al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from Abu Ishaq, from Hanash ibn al-Mutamir, from Abu Dharr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My household among you are like the ship of Noah, upon him be peace, among his people; whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays back from it perishes. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar."
"5397","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Dabbagh narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hakam ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Abu Isam, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear white; let your living wear it, and shroud your dead in it. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; al-Husayn ibn al-Hakam was alone in narrating it."
"5398","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abi Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, who said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, became angry with a man, so I said: Shall I strike his neck? He said: That was for no one after Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5399","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythama narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abi Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mughira narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Rabi ibn Abi Rashid, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, who said: I said to my father: Who is the best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. No one narrated these two hadiths from Malik ibn Mighwal except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira."
"5400","Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Sudai narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, who said: A man came to Abdullah ibn Masud and said: Which deeds are best? He said: You have asked me about what I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about, and he said: Prayer at its time, kindness to parents, and striving in the cause of Allah; had I asked him for more he would have given me more. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Hammad ibn al-Walid."
